window.EXAM_DATA = {"id":"cca-scenario-b","title":"시나리오 모의고사 B","subtitle":"Scenario Mock B · 60 Questions","kind":"mock","timeLimitSec":7200,"passScaled":720,"domains":{"1":"Agentic Architecture & Orchestration","2":"Tool Design & MCP Integration","3":"Claude Code Configuration & Workflows","4":"Prompt Engineering & Structured Output","5":"Context Management & Reliability"},"domainWeights":{"1":27,"2":18,"3":20,"4":20,"5":15},"domainShort":{"1":"Agentic","2":"Tools & MCP","3":"Claude Code","4":"Prompting","5":"Context"},"note":"자체 제작 CCAR-F 연습 문제입니다(비공식). 문제·보기는 영어, 해설은 한국어. 이 도구의 점수식은 공식 채점과 다릅니다.","questions":[{"domain":1,"stem":"Before migrating fully to the Agent SDK, Wayfinder's \"quick-explain\" command still uses a hand-written loop over the Messages API. Engineers report that explanations often stop right after Claude says something like \"Let me look at the invoice mapper first.\" The loop looks like this:\n\nwhile True:\n    resp = client.messages.create(model=MODEL, tools=TOOLS, messages=msgs, max_tokens=4096)\n    msgs.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": resp.content})\n    if any(b.type == \"text\" for b in resp.content):\n        return final_text(resp)          # treat any text as the answer\n    msgs.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": run_tools(resp.content)})\n\nWhat is the most effective fix?","options":["Raise `max_tokens` substantially so Claude can finish all of its reasoning in a single response before it decides to emit any tool calls, which keeps the text check working as intended.","Add a system-prompt rule telling Claude never to write narrative text in the same response as a tool call, so the existing text check only fires once the explanation is truly complete.","Set `tool_choice` to `{\"type\": \"any\"}` on every request so that Claude always emits a tool call instead of narration, and treat the first response without tool calls as the final answer.","Drive the loop from `stop_reason`: while it is `\"tool_use\"`, run every tool_use block, append the matching tool_result blocks, and call again; exit only when it is `\"end_turn\"`."],"answer":3,"explanation":"이 루프의 근본 원인은 \"응답에 text 블록이 있으면 끝\"이라는 잘못된 종료 조건입니다. Claude는 한 응답 안에 설명 text와 tool_use 블록을 함께 낼 수 있으므로, text 존재 여부는 작업 완료 신호가 아닙니다. agentic loop의 올바른 제어 신호는 `stop_reason`입니다. `\"tool_use\"`이면 모든 tool_use 블록을 실행하고 같은 `id`에 대응하는 tool_result를 user 메시지로 돌려준 뒤 다시 호출하고, `\"end_turn\"`일 때 종료합니다. 코드 버그를 프롬프트나 파라미터로 우회하지 말고 루프 제어 로직 자체를 고쳐야 합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 루프 계속/종료는 응답 내용 추측이 아니라 `stop_reason`으로 판단 — Task Statement 1.1 · 출처: Section 2 (L4, L6)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: `max_tokens`는 `stop_reason: \"max_tokens\"` 문제를 다룰 때의 레버입니다. text와 tool_use가 섞이는 정상 동작은 그대로이므로 조기 종료가 계속됩니다.\n- B: 결정적 코드 버그를 확률적 프롬프트로 덮는 방식입니다. 모델이 가끔 지시를 어기면 같은 실패가 재발합니다.\n- C: `any`는 매 턴 도구 호출을 강제하므로 `end_turn`으로 자연스럽게 끝날 수 없고, 최종 답을 쓸 수 없는 루프를 만듭니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"text가 있으면 종료\", \"도구 호출이 없으면 종료\" 같은 휴리스틱 대신 `stop_reason`을 고르세요.","id":"scenario-b-1","task":"1.1","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":2,"stem":"An engineer asks Wayfinder: \"Where is `PaymentRouter` actually instantiated in the billing core?\" The session's tool log shows `Bash: find billing -name \"*.java\" | xargs cat | grep -n PaymentRouter`, followed by sequential Read calls on 58 whole files. The run consumed most of the context window and cost ten times the team's per-question budget. What should Wayfinder do instead?","options":["Call Glob with a pattern such as `billing/**/*PaymentRouter*.java`, then Read each matching file in full, because file names in the billing core reliably reflect where each class gets constructed.","Keep the Bash pipeline but append `| head -100` to every shell command, so the output that lands in context stays short while still covering all of the matching source lines.","Call Grep with a pattern like `new PaymentRouter\\(` limited to `*.java` files under `billing/`, then Read only the matched files around the reported line numbers to confirm each construction site.","Add a custom MCP tool backed by an embeddings index of the monorepo, and route every symbol question through semantic search instead of using any of the built-in file tools."],"answer":2,"explanation":"질문은 \"어디서 생성(instantiate)되는가\"라는 파일 내용 검색이므로 built-in Grep이 정확한 도구입니다. 정규식 패턴과 파일 유형/경로 필터로 일치하는 위치만 돌려받고, 그 뒤 Read로 해당 파일의 관련 구간만 확인하면 컨텍스트와 비용이 크게 줄어듭니다. `find | xargs cat`처럼 Bash로 전체 파일을 쏟아붓는 방식은 전용 도구를 우회하면서 불필요한 텍스트를 컨텍스트에 넣습니다. 전체 파일을 순차적으로 읽는 것도 같은 낭비입니다. task-driven tool selection: 이름 패턴은 Glob, 내용 패턴은 Grep, 확인은 Read입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 내용 검색 = Grep, 파일명 패턴 = Glob, 상세 확인 = 타깃 Read — Task Statement 2.5 · 출처: Section 9 (L59), Section 8 (L56)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: Glob은 파일 이름 패턴을 찾습니다. 클래스가 생성되는 곳은 다른 이름의 파일들이므로 엉뚱한 파일(정의 파일)만 찾게 됩니다.\n- B: 출력을 잘라도 Bash로 전체 파일을 읽는 비효율은 그대로이고, `head`가 실제 일치 결과를 잘라 버려 누락이 생깁니다.\n- D: 정확한 기호 검색에 built-in Grep으로 충분한데 임베딩 인덱스를 새로 만드는 것은 과잉 설계이며, 의미 검색은 정확한 생성 위치에 오히려 덜 정밀합니다.\n\n시험 팁: Claude Code/Agent SDK에는 Grep·Glob 전용 도구가 있으니, Bash로 grep/find/cat을 돌리는 선택지는 대개 오답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-2","task":"2.5","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":1,"stem":"After a 30-minute conversation in which an engineer and the main agent narrowed a bug to `billing/settlement/` and ruled out the currency converter, the main agent delegates with this prompt: \"Investigate the settlement bug we discussed and find the root cause.\" The `explorer` subagent returns a long report about the currency converter and an unrelated module. What is the best fix?","options":["Give `explorer` the same full tool set as the main agent, including Bash and the `jira` MCP tools, so that it can look up the ticket and recover the missing background by itself.","Raise `explorer`'s `max_turns` and remove its read-only restriction so that it can keep investigating until it eventually reaches the module the engineer and the main agent had narrowed down.","Write the delegation prompt with the needed facts: the target path, the failing invoice ID and error code, what has already been ruled out, and the exact shape of the report to return.","Configure `explorer` to resume the main agent's `session_id` when it starts, so that it inherits the full conversation history and already knows what the engineer and agent discussed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"subagent는 독립된 새 컨텍스트에서 시작하며 부모 대화를 상속하지 않습니다. 그래서 \"우리가 논의한 버그\"라는 표현은 subagent에게 아무 정보도 주지 않습니다. 부모가 할 일은 delegation prompt 안에 목표, 범위(경로), 이미 확인·배제한 것, 구체적 식별자(invoice ID, error code), return format을 명시적으로 넣는 것입니다. 이것이 context passing의 핵심이며, 반환 형식을 정하면 부모가 결과를 검증하기도 쉬워집니다. 문제는 도구나 턴 수가 아니라 정보 전달입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: subagent는 부모 대화를 모름 → 필요한 사실과 반환 계약을 프롬프트에 명시 — Task Statement 1.3 · 출처: Section 4 (L17), Section 18 (L123)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 도구를 넓히면 최소 권한 원칙을 깨고, 티켓에는 대화에서 좁힌 결론(배제한 모듈)이 없으므로 근본 원인이 해결되지 않습니다.\n- B: 방향 정보가 없는 탐색을 더 오래 하게 할 뿐이며, 쓰기 권한 해제는 위험만 늘립니다.\n- D: 부모 세션 전체를 이어받으면 subagent를 쓰는 이유인 컨텍스트 격리가 사라지고, 큰 기록이 그대로 비용과 잡음이 됩니다.\n\n시험 팁: subagent 결과가 엉뚱하면 먼저 \"프롬프트에 필요한 컨텍스트를 명시적으로 넘겼는가\"를 의심하세요.","id":"scenario-b-3","task":"1.3","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":1,"stem":"`legacy_index` returns symbol locations as SVN-era absolute paths such as `/svn/trunk/billing/src/Ledger.java` with 0-based line numbers, while the repository uses repo-relative paths and Read uses 1-based lines. Wayfinder frequently Reads the wrong lines or fails with \"file not found.\" The tooling team will NOT change the server's output because other consumers depend on it. What is the best design?","options":["Add detailed instructions to Wayfinder's system prompt explaining the path prefix and the off-by-one line convention, and ask Claude to convert each location carefully before calling Read.","Register a PostToolUse hook matching `mcp__legacy_index__.*` that rewrites each returned location to a repo-relative path with a 1-based line number before the result reaches the model.","Register a PreToolUse hook on Read that rejects any call whose path starts with `/svn/trunk/`, returning a reason that tells Claude to fix the path and line number and then retry the call.","Remove `legacy_index` from Wayfinder entirely and have the agent locate symbols only with Grep, because built-in tools return paths and line numbers in the format Read expects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"서버 출력을 바꿀 수 없을 때 heterogeneous data를 모델이 보기 전에 정규화하는 표준 위치가 PostToolUse hook입니다. matcher를 `mcp__legacy_index__.*`로 걸면 이 서버의 모든 결과에 결정적으로(deterministic) 같은 변환이 적용되어, 모델은 항상 repo 기준 경로와 1-based 줄 번호만 보게 됩니다. 이 방식은 모델의 변환 실수 가능성을 없애고 다른 소비자에게도 영향을 주지 않습니다. 매번 반드시 일어나야 하는 데이터 변환은 프롬프트가 아니라 코드로 처리합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 도구 결과 정규화 = PostToolUse hook (모델이 보기 전, 매번 결정적으로) — Task Statement 1.5 · 출처: Section 5 (L30), Section 12 Part 2 S1\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 확률적 지시라서 변환 실수가 계속 남고, 모든 호출마다 모델이 산술을 해야 하므로 신뢰성이 낮습니다.\n- C: 잘못된 호출을 막을 뿐 변환은 여전히 모델이 해야 하며, 줄 번호 오류(경로는 맞고 줄만 틀린 경우)는 잡지 못합니다. 재시도 왕복 비용도 늘어납니다.\n- D: 정규화 문제 때문에 정밀한 symbol 인덱스(정의/참조 정보)를 버리는 것은 기능 손실이 큰 과잉 대응입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"서버는 못 바꾸고, 형식이 제각각인 결과를 모델 앞에서 맞춰야 한다\" → PostToolUse 정규화를 고르세요.","id":"scenario-b-4","task":"1.5","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Wayfinder's system prompt and the repository's CLAUDE.md both state that `scaffolder` must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`. An audit of 4,000 runs found 11 Write or Edit calls into `generated/`, two of which were overwritten by the next codegen run and silently lost hand edits. What should the team implement?","options":["A PreToolUse hook matching `Write|Edit` that resolves `tool_input.file_path`, denies any call inside the protected directories, and returns a reason so `scaffolder` can pick an allowed location.","A stronger CLAUDE.md rule written in capital letters, with two worked examples showing where generated code belongs, and the same rule repeated at the end of the `scaffolder` system prompt.","A PostToolUse hook matching `Write|Edit` that detects a protected path, restores the file with `git checkout`, and then tells `scaffolder` that its change was reverted and must be redone elsewhere.","Removing Write and Edit from `scaffolder` altogether, so that it only prints proposed file contents into Slack and an engineer copies each generated file into the repository by hand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"감사 결과는 프롬프트와 CLAUDE.md 지시가 확률적이라 드물게 위반된다는 것을 보여 줍니다. \"절대 일어나면 안 되는\" 규칙은 PreToolUse hook으로 실행 전에 강제해야 합니다. hook이 `file_path`를 정규화(심볼릭 링크, `..` 처리)한 뒤 보호 경로면 deny하고 이유를 돌려주면, 쓰기는 일어나지 않고 `scaffolder`는 그 피드백으로 올바른 위치를 고를 수 있습니다. 이것이 deterministic enforcement 패턴이며, 기능(쓰기 능력)은 유지하면서 위반만 차단합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 반드시 막아야 하는 행동 = PreToolUse에서 실행 전 차단 — Task Statement 1.5 · 출처: Section 5 (L28–L30), Section 12 Part 2 S1\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 이미 실패한 방식(프롬프트 지시)을 강하게 반복할 뿐이며, 확률을 낮출 수는 있어도 0으로 만들지 못합니다.\n- C: PostToolUse는 도구가 이미 실행된 뒤라 쓰기를 막지 못합니다. 되돌리기 사이에 codegen이나 다른 프로세스와 경쟁 상태가 생길 수 있고, 추적되지 않은 파일은 `git checkout`으로 복원되지 않습니다.\n- D: 위반률 0.3%를 막으려고 핵심 기능인 자동 생성을 없애는 과잉 대응입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"프롬프트 규칙이 가끔 깨진다 + 결과가 치명적\" → PreToolUse 차단, PostToolUse는 사후 피드백용입니다.","id":"scenario-b-5","task":"1.5","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":1,"stem":"An engineer spent 45 minutes with Wayfinder mapping how the legacy `ChargeCalculator` is wired into four services. She now wants two competing migration write-ups produced from that same understanding — one using a strangler-fig facade and one using a direct rewrite — and wants to compare them side by side. Both are text-only plans; no files will be edited. How should Wayfinder run this?","options":["Take the stored `session_id` and start each write-up with `resume` set to that ID and `fork_session=True`, so each write-up branches into its own new session from the exploration state while the original stays intact.","Resume the original session for the facade write-up, then resume the same session again for the rewrite, so that both write-ups reuse the stored exploration history from the same `session_id`.","Use `continue_conversation=True` for each write-up, so that the SDK automatically picks up the most recent session and both alternatives build on the exploration without managing IDs.","Start two fresh sessions and paste a one-paragraph summary of the exploration into each prompt, so that the two write-ups are fully independent and neither one inherits any accumulated history."],"answer":0,"explanation":"같은 출발점에서 두 가지 대안을 따로 탐색하는 것이 session forking의 전형적 용도입니다. `resume=<session_id>`와 `fork_session=True`를 함께 쓰면 그 시점의 대화 상태를 복사한 새 session ID로 분기하므로, 두 write-up이 서로의 내용을 보지 않고 원래 탐색 세션도 그대로 남습니다. 45분 동안 쌓은 상세한 탐색 결과(파일, 호출 관계)를 두 갈래 모두 그대로 활용할 수 있다는 것이 핵심 이점입니다. 이 문제에서는 파일 편집이 없으므로 fork가 파일시스템을 분리하지 않는다는 한계도 문제가 되지 않습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 같은 상태에서 대안 두 개 = resume + fork_session — Task Statement 1.7 · 출처: Section 12 (L81, Part 2 S2)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: fork 없이 같은 세션을 다시 resume하면 두 번째 write-up이 첫 번째 write-up의 대화까지 이어받아 서로 오염됩니다.\n- C: `continue_conversation`은 가장 최근 세션을 이어갑니다. 두 번째 실행은 첫 번째 대안의 세션을 이어받게 되어 B와 같은 문제가 생깁니다.\n- D: 한 문단 요약은 탐색의 세부 사항(경로, 호출 지점)을 잃어 다시 탐색해야 하므로 비용과 품질이 모두 나빠집니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"같은 지점에서 갈라져 비교\" → fork, \"어제 하던 일을 이어서\" → resume로 구분하세요.","id":"scenario-b-6","task":"1.7","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":5,"stem":"When engineers ask broad questions such as \"How does a shipment get from booking to invoice?\", Wayfinder's main agent runs dozens of Grep and Read calls itself. By the time it starts answering, roughly 70% of the context is raw search output, and engineers notice that follow-up questions in the same session get vaguer answers that forget details stated earlier. What is the most effective change?","options":["Move Wayfinder to a model with a larger context window, so that the raw search output from broad questions fits comfortably and earlier conversation details are no longer pushed out.","Append `| head -50` to the agent's searches and instruct it to Read at most 100 lines per file, so that each tool result stays small no matter how broad the engineer's question is.","Run `/compact` automatically every ten tool calls during broad questions, so that the accumulated search output is summarized and space is freed before the agent writes its answer.","Delegate broad discovery to the read-only `explorer` subagent, which searches in its own context and returns a concise report of the relevant files, line references, and flow."],"answer":3,"explanation":"넓은 codebase exploration은 본질적으로 장황한(verbose) 작업이라, 메인 컨텍스트에서 직접 하면 원본 검색 결과가 쌓여 이후 추론의 품질이 떨어집니다. 해결책은 discovery를 subagent에 위임하는 것입니다. `explorer`가 자신의 격리된 컨텍스트에서 Grep/Read를 수행하고, 메인 에이전트에는 경로와 줄 번호가 담긴 간결한 결과만 돌려줍니다. 메인 컨텍스트에는 결론만 남으므로 이후 질문에 대한 답의 정확도가 유지됩니다. 이미 정의된 read-only subagent를 쓰는 것이므로 추가 비용도 작습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 장황한 탐색은 subagent에 격리, 메인에는 요약된 결과만 — Task Statement 5.4 · 출처: Section 18 (L122), Section 16 (L112)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 더 큰 창은 문제 시점을 미룰 뿐이며, 관련 없는 토큰이 많을수록 주의가 분산되는 품질 저하는 그대로입니다.\n- B: 결과를 기계적으로 자르면 필요한 일치 항목과 코드가 누락되고, 넓은 질문에서는 호출 수가 늘어 결국 다시 쌓입니다.\n- C: compaction은 손실 있는 요약이라 세부 사항(정확한 경로, 값)을 잃기 쉽고, 노이즈를 먼저 넣은 뒤 치우는 사후 처리입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"탐색 출력이 메인 컨텍스트를 채운다\" → explorer subagent 위임 + 간결한 반환이 정답 패턴입니다.","id":"scenario-b-7","task":"5.4","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The team adds the remote `jira` MCP server to Wayfinder's `ClaudeAgentOptions` through `mcp_servers`. The SDK init message lists the tools `mcp__jira__get_issue` and `mcp__jira__add_comment`, but every attempt to call them in the Slack bot (which has no interactive permission prompt) ends in a permission denial. The options currently include `allowed_tools=[\"Read\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Edit\", \"Write\"]`. What is the best fix?","options":["Switch the `jira` server from its remote HTTP transport to a local stdio process, because tools served over stdio are trusted by default and therefore do not go through the permission checks.","Add the Jira tools to `allowed_tools` by their full MCP names, such as `mcp__jira__get_issue` and `mcp__jira__add_comment`, so the non-interactive bot can use exactly those tools.","Set `permission_mode=\"bypassPermissions\"` for the Slack bot, so that every tool call, including the Jira tools and any MCP tools added later, runs without hitting a permission check.","Rename the server's tools to short names such as `get_issue` and `add_comment` in the server code, so that they match the plain style of the built-in tools already listed in `allowed_tools`."],"answer":1,"explanation":"서버 연결은 정상이고(init 메시지에 도구가 보임), 문제는 권한 설정입니다. MCP 도구는 `mcp__<server>__<tool>` 형식의 이름으로 노출되며, 비대화형 환경에서 사전 허용 목록에 없는 도구는 승인받을 방법이 없어 거부됩니다. 필요한 Jira 도구를 전체 이름으로 `allowed_tools`에 추가하면 정확히 그 도구만 허용되어 least privilege도 지켜집니다. MCP 통합 문제에서는 \"연결 문제인가, 권한 문제인가\"를 먼저 구분하는 것이 중요합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: MCP 도구 허용은 `mcp__server__tool` 이름으로 명시 — Task Statement 2.4 · 출처: Section 12 Part 2 S2, Section 8 (L54)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: transport는 연결 방식일 뿐 권한 검사를 면제하지 않습니다. 원격 서버를 로컬로 바꾸는 것은 배포 구조만 흔듭니다.\n- C: 동작은 하지만 Bash와 Write를 포함한 모든 도구의 권한 검사를 끄는 과도한 조치로, 격리된 sandbox 밖에서는 부적절합니다.\n- D: SDK가 MCP 도구에 서버 접두사를 붙이므로 서버 쪽 이름을 바꿔도 노출 이름은 여전히 `mcp__jira__...`이며 권한 문제는 남습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 도구는 보이는데 호출이 거부되면 연결이 아니라 allow 목록과 MCP 도구 이름 형식을 확인하세요.","id":"scenario-b-8","task":"2.4","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":2,"stem":"Many Tidemark engineers also use Claude Code directly in the monorepo, and the platform team wants every one of them to get the `legacy_index` MCP server automatically when they open the repository. The server needs a per-engineer API token that must never be committed. Which configuration is best?","options":["Have each engineer run `claude mcp add` at user scope with their own token, and document the exact command in the repository README so that new joiners copy it during their onboarding.","Commit a project `.mcp.json` that contains the server definition with the platform team's shared service token written directly into it, so that every engineer is configured the moment they clone.","Commit a project `.mcp.json` with the server definition and reference the token through environment-variable expansion, such as `${LEGACY_INDEX_TOKEN}`, which each engineer sets locally.","Add the server definition to the repository's root CLAUDE.md along with instructions for Claude to connect to it, so that it loads automatically for every engineer who opens the repo."],"answer":2,"explanation":"팀 전체가 공유해야 하는 MCP 서버는 project scope의 `.mcp.json`에 정의해 저장소에 커밋하는 것이 표준입니다. 비밀 값은 파일에 직접 쓰지 않고 environment variable expansion(`${VAR}`)으로 참조하면, 정의는 공유하면서 토큰은 각자 로컬 환경에 둘 수 있습니다. 이 방식으로 \"자동 공유\"와 \"비밀 미커밋\"이라는 두 요구를 동시에 만족합니다. 프로젝트 MCP 서버는 처음 사용할 때 사용자 승인을 거치므로 신뢰 경계도 유지됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 팀 공유 = 프로젝트 `.mcp.json`, 비밀 = 환경 변수 확장 — Task Statement 2.4 · 출처: Section 8 (L55), Section 9 (L61)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: user scope는 개인 설정이라 자동 공유되지 않고, README 복사 의존은 누락과 불일치를 낳습니다.\n- B: 비밀을 저장소에 커밋하는 보안 위반이며, 공유 토큰은 개인별 감사(audit)도 불가능하게 합니다.\n- D: CLAUDE.md는 지시와 컨텍스트를 담는 파일이지 MCP 서버를 등록하는 설정 메커니즘이 아닙니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"팀 전원 자동 + 비밀 미커밋\" → `.mcp.json`(project) + `${ENV_VAR}` 조합을 기억하세요.","id":"scenario-b-9","task":"2.4","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Wayfinder receives two kinds of write requests in the same week: (1) dozens of requests like \"generate a DTO and a test stub for the new `PalletScan` event\" that each create one or two new files, and (2) one request to replace the deprecated `LegacyMoney` type, which is used in about 140 files across the billing core and three Go services, many with thin tests. How should Wayfinder's execution modes be configured?","options":["Use plan mode for every write request, including the single-file DTO scaffolds, so that engineers always get the same uniform review gate before any file changes are made anywhere.","Use direct execution with `acceptEdits` for both kinds of request, relying on the CI test suite to catch any mistakes after the changes land in the engineer's working branch.","Use plan mode for the DTO scaffolds because they create brand-new files, and direct execution for the `LegacyMoney` replacement because it only edits files that already exist.","Use plan mode for the `LegacyMoney` replacement and review its files and risks before approving, and use direct execution for the small, easily reversible single-file scaffolds."],"answer":3,"explanation":"plan mode는 실행 전에 단계, 대상 파일, 위험과 가정을 드러내는 read-only 단계 + approval gate입니다. 수많은 파일과 여러 서비스에 걸치고, 테스트가 얇아 되돌리기 어려운 `LegacyMoney` 교체는 plan mode가 가장 가치 있는 경우입니다. 반대로 새 파일 한두 개를 만드는 작은 scaffold는 실수 비용이 낮고 쉽게 되돌릴 수 있어 direct execution이 더 효율적입니다. 결정 기준은 \"항상/절대\"가 아니라 작업의 위험 프로필(범위, 가역성)입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 여러 모듈·되돌리기 어려움 → plan mode, 작고 가역적인 단일 파일 → direct — Task Statement 3.4 · 출처: Section 11 (L78, L79)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 모든 요청에 승인 관문을 두면 수십 건의 사소한 작업에 오버헤드가 쌓이고, 리뷰 피로로 정작 중요한 plan을 대충 승인하게 됩니다.\n- B: 테스트가 얇은 레거시 영역에서는 CI가 오류를 잡는다는 전제가 성립하지 않으며, 140개 파일에 걸친 잘못된 가정은 사후에 풀기 매우 비쌉니다.\n- C: 기준이 뒤집혔습니다. \"새 파일인가\"가 아니라 영향 범위와 가역성이 판단 기준입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"10초면 되돌릴 실수\"는 direct, \"30분 이상 걸릴 실수\"는 plan mode로 판단하세요.","id":"scenario-b-10","task":"3.4","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":5,"stem":"During a three-hour debugging session on the billing core, the engineer established several facts: the rounding mode must stay `HALF_EVEN`, the failing invoices are `INV-88213` and `INV-88240`, and the error code is `BL-4471`. After the session was compacted twice, Wayfinder proposed a fix that switches to `HALF_UP` and cited the error code as `BL-4417`. What is the most effective way to prevent this?","options":["Keep a structured fact block of confirmed constraints and exact identifiers outside the summarized history, update it as facts are confirmed, and re-inject it into every turn so compaction cannot erode it.","Instruct the agent to write longer and more thorough summaries whenever compaction happens, explicitly asking it to preserve any numbers, identifiers, and constraints mentioned earlier in the session.","Move Wayfinder to a model with a much larger context window, so that compaction is triggered far less often during long debugging sessions and the original messages stay intact.","Ask engineers to put all critical constraints into the very first message of each session, written in capital letters, so that the summarizer treats them as the most important content to keep."],"answer":0,"explanation":"요약(compaction)은 유창함을 위해 구체성을 희생하는 경향이 있어, 숫자, 식별자, 제약 조건 같은 정확한 값이 가장 먼저 손실되거나 변형됩니다(`BL-4471` → `BL-4417`). 해결책은 이런 값을 요약 대상 대화에서 분리해 persistent fact block으로 관리하는 것입니다. 사실이 확인될 때마다 블록을 갱신하고 매 턴 다시 주입하면 요약이 몇 번 반복되어도 원문 그대로 유지됩니다. 이것이 extract-first 패턴의 핵심입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 정확한 값과 제약은 요약에 맡기지 말고 별도 fact block으로 보존·재주입 — Task Statement 5.1 · 출처: Section 16 (L109, L110)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 요약이 길어져도 요약의 본질적 손실은 남고, 반복되는 요약 단계마다 오류가 누적됩니다.\n- C: compaction 시점을 늦출 뿐이며, 세 시간짜리 세션에서는 결국 같은 손실이 발생합니다.\n- D: 첫 메시지도 대화 기록의 일부라 함께 요약되며, 대문자 강조가 보존을 보장하지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 요약 후 숫자·ID·제약이 틀어지면 → \"요약을 더 잘하게\"가 아니라 \"요약 밖으로 빼서 고정\"이 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-11","task":"5.1","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":2,"stem":"`scaffolder` was asked to change the payments timeout in `deploy/services.yaml`, a 1,900-line file in which `timeout: 30` appears in four different service sections. Its Edit call failed because `old_string` matched more than one location, so it fell back to Write with the whole file regenerated from memory. The new file silently dropped two comment blocks and a trailing service definition. What should Wayfinder's tool guidance be?","options":["Retry the failed Edit with an `old_string` that includes enough surrounding lines, such as the payments section header, to match exactly once, and reserve Write for creating new files.","Prefer Write for every configuration change, because regenerating the complete file is deterministic and avoids the uniqueness errors that Edit raises whenever a string repeats in the file.","Switch to a Bash `sed -i` command that targets the specific line number of the payments timeout, since a line-number edit is never ambiguous even when the same text repeats in a file.","Set `replace_all=true` on the Edit call whenever the first attempt fails because of a uniqueness error, so the change is applied cleanly without having to rebuild a longer `old_string`."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Edit는 `old_string`이 파일에서 정확히 한 번 일치해야 적용되는 안전한 부분 수정 도구입니다. 일치가 여러 곳이면 실패하는 것은 의도된 안전장치이며, 올바른 대응은 섹션 헤더 같은 주변 줄을 포함해 고유하게 만든 뒤 재시도하는 것입니다. Write는 파일 전체를 덮어쓰므로 기존 대형 파일 수정에 쓰면 기억에 의존한 재생성 과정에서 내용이 조용히 사라집니다. Write는 새 파일 생성이나 의도적인 전체 교체에만 써야 합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 기존 파일 부분 수정 = Edit(고유한 old_string), Write = 새 파일/전체 교체 — Task Statement 2.5 · 출처: Section 9 (L59)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 이번 사고의 원인이 바로 Write 전체 재생성이므로 같은 손실을 정책으로 만드는 셈입니다.\n- C: 줄 번호는 파일이 바뀌면 쉽게 어긋나고, Bash `sed`는 Edit의 일치 검증을 우회하므로 엉뚱한 줄을 조용히 바꿀 수 있습니다.\n- D: `replace_all`은 네 서비스의 timeout을 모두 바꿔 버립니다. 모든 일치를 바꾸려는 의도가 있을 때만 씁니다.\n\n시험 팁: Edit의 \"not unique\" 오류에 대한 정답은 더 넓은 문맥으로 재시도이지 Write나 replace_all이 아닙니다.","id":"scenario-b-12","task":"2.5","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Engineers complain that `scaffolder`'s gRPC handler boilerplate never quite matches house conventions: wrong error-wrapping style, missing tracing spans, and test files in the wrong package. They have been re-prompting with feedback like \"make it more idiomatic\" and \"follow our style,\" and each round fixes one thing while breaking another. What is the most effective way to iterate toward correct output?","options":["Expand `scaffolder`'s system prompt with stronger descriptive guidance, such as \"write clean, idiomatic, production-quality Go that follows all Tidemark conventions,\" and repeat it at the top of every request.","Generate five candidate handlers for every request at a higher sampling temperature, and let the engineer choose whichever candidate happens to look closest to the house conventions each time.","Give `scaffolder` two approved handlers as concrete input-to-output examples plus a test suite the new handler must pass, then iterate by feeding back the specific failing checks each round.","Let engineers hand-fix each generated handler and commit it, so that over time `scaffolder` picks up the corrected patterns from the repository and converges on the conventions by itself."],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"더 idiomatic하게\" 같은 모호한 피드백은 기준이 없어 매 라운드마다 다른 해석을 낳고, 하나를 고치면 다른 것이 깨지는 진동이 생깁니다. iterative refinement를 효과적으로 하려면 구체적 예시(concrete input/output examples)로 목표를 보여 주고, 테스트처럼 검증 가능한 기준을 먼저 정한 뒤, 실패한 항목을 구체적으로 피드백하는 루프를 돌려야 합니다. 이렇게 하면 각 라운드의 개선이 누적되고, 이미 통과한 항목이 깨지면 바로 드러납니다. 승인된 핸들러 예시는 오류 래핑, tracing, 패키지 구조를 한 번에 전달합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 모호한 형용사 대신 예시 + 테스트 + 구체적 실패 피드백으로 반복 — Task Statement 3.5 · 출처: Section 11 (L79), Section 13\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 형용사 위주의 지시는 정밀도가 낮아 \"Tidemark 컨벤션\"이 무엇인지 여전히 알려 주지 못합니다.\n- B: 무작위성을 늘려 운에 맡기는 방식으로, 기준이 없으니 수렴하지 않고 리뷰 부담만 커집니다.\n- D: 모델은 커밋에서 스스로 학습하지 않습니다. 예시를 명시적으로 컨텍스트에 넣지 않으면 개선이 반영되지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 반복 개선 문제에서는 \"구체적 예시 / 테스트 기준 / 구체적 피드백\"이 들어간 선택지를 찾으세요.","id":"scenario-b-13","task":"3.5","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":1,"stem":"On Monday an engineer and Wayfinder analyzed 40 files in the routing service and agreed on a refactoring approach. Overnight, teammates merged commits that changed 3 of those 40 files. On Tuesday the Slack bot resumes Monday's session by its stored `session_id`, and Wayfinder confidently edits code based on the Monday versions of those 3 files, producing broken changes. What should the resume flow do?","options":["Resume the session with an extra instruction to \"carefully continue where we left off,\" since resuming restores the full conversation including all of Monday's analysis of the routing service files.","Resume the session, then inject a message listing the files changed since Monday (from the git diff) and instruct Wayfinder to re-read those files before continuing, treating its earlier reads of them as stale.","Fork Monday's session instead of resuming it, so that the original analysis remains untouched and Tuesday's work happens in a new branch that no longer depends on yesterday's file contents.","Discard Monday's session every morning and start a fresh session that re-explores all 40 files from scratch, since any resumed conversation may contain tool results that are already out of date."],"answer":1,"explanation":"session resume는 대화 상태를 복원할 뿐 파일시스템의 변화를 반영하지 않습니다. 그래서 Monday의 tool result(파일 내용)는 그대로 남아 있고, 모델은 이를 현재 상태로 믿고 행동합니다. 올바른 재개는 무엇이 바뀌었는지 명시적으로 알려 주고(git diff 기반 변경 파일 목록), 해당 파일만 다시 읽게 해서 오래된 결과를 교체하는 것입니다. 이렇게 하면 변경되지 않은 37개 파일에 대한 분석은 재사용하면서 stale state로 인한 오류만 막을 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: resume는 대화만 복원 → 바뀐 환경을 알리고 해당 부분만 재검증 — Task Statement 1.7 · 출처: Section 4 (L22), Section 12 Part 2 S2\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 바로 이번 실패의 원인입니다. \"조심히\" 같은 지시는 모델이 파일이 바뀌었다는 사실을 알게 해 주지 않습니다.\n- C: fork도 같은 대화 기록(Monday 파일 내용)을 복사하므로 staleness 문제가 그대로입니다. fork는 대안 비교용입니다.\n- D: 일부만 바뀐 상황에서 매일 전부 다시 탐색하는 것은 비용이 큰 과잉 대응입니다(대부분의 파일이 바뀐 경우라면 새 세션 + 요약이 나을 수 있음).\n\n시험 팁: \"resume 후 오래된 정보로 자신 있게 틀린다\" → 변경 사항을 주입하고 타깃 재검증하는 선택지를 고르세요.","id":"scenario-b-14","task":"1.7","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A two-engineer team is spending three weeks reverse-engineering the legacy `RateEngine` module with Wayfinder, starting a new session each morning. Every session spends its first hour rediscovering the same entry points, re-testing two hypotheses that were already disproven, and missing a key quirk found on day two. What is the best approach?","options":["Enable `continue_conversation` so that each morning simply continues the previous day's session, letting the whole three weeks of exploration accumulate in one ever-growing conversation.","Append every finding from each session to the repository's root CLAUDE.md, so that all future sessions across the whole monorepo automatically load the accumulated `RateEngine` knowledge.","Rely on the SDK's automatic compaction, which summarizes earlier turns of the session, so that the important discoveries from previous days are carried forward into each new morning's session.","Keep a structured findings file for `RateEngine` with confirmed facts and their paths, open questions, and dead ends; have Wayfinder read it at session start and update it before ending."],"answer":3,"explanation":"여러 날에 걸친 large codebase exploration에서는 매 세션이 빈 상태로 시작하므로, 발견 사항을 세션 밖의 durable한 scratchpad 파일에 남겨야 합니다. 확인된 사실(경로·줄 번호 포함), 열린 질문, 이미 배제한 가설(dead ends)로 구조화하면 같은 탐색과 반증된 가설의 재시험을 막을 수 있습니다. 세션 시작 시 읽고 종료 전에 갱신하는 흐름을 강제하고(예: hook이나 고정 워크플로), 크기를 관리하며 오래된 항목을 정리해야 신뢰할 수 있습니다. 두 엔지니어가 같은 파일을 공유하므로 팀 단위의 지식도 일관되게 유지됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 세션을 넘는 탐색 지식 = 구조화된 scratchpad 파일(읽기·쓰기 강제) — Task Statement 5.4 · 출처: Section 18 (L120, L121)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 3주 분량을 한 세션에 쌓으면 컨텍스트가 비대해지고 반복 compaction으로 세부 사항이 손실되며, 두 번째 엔지니어와의 공유도 안 됩니다.\n- B: CLAUDE.md는 안정적인 규칙·컨벤션용입니다. 일시적이고 자주 바뀌는 탐색 기록을 넣으면 모든 세션에 불필요한 컨텍스트 비용을 지우는 경계 위반입니다.\n- C: compaction은 한 세션 안에서만 동작하며 새 세션으로 지식을 넘겨주지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"매 세션 같은 것을 다시 발견한다\" → scratchpad 파일, \"모든 세션에 늘 필요한 규칙\" → CLAUDE.md로 구분하세요.","id":"scenario-b-15","task":"5.4","scenario":"Developer Productivity with Claude","scenarioIntro":"Tidemark Freight, a mid-sized logistics company, runs a 2.3-million-line monorepo that mixes a 15-year-old Java 8 billing core, a dozen Go microservices, and a TypeScript operations console. The platform team built Wayfinder, an internal developer-productivity assistant written in Python on the Claude Agent SDK, which engineers reach through a Slack bot and a thin CLI wrapper. Wayfinder's main agent has the built-in Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, and Write tools, and it can delegate to two programmatically defined subagents: `explorer` (read-only: Read, Grep, Glob) for codebase discovery and `scaffolder` (Read, Write, Edit) for generating boilerplate such as DTOs, handlers, and test stubs. Two MCP servers are attached: `legacy_index`, an external server owned by a separate tooling team that wraps a vendor symbol indexer used by several other internal consumers, and `jira`, a remote server that reads and comments on tickets. Each engineer's work is a separate SDK session whose `session_id` is stored by the Slack bot so that conversations can be resumed the next day. Hard constraints: Wayfinder must never write into `vendor/`, `generated/`, or `secrets/`; the billing core has thin test coverage and contains money-rounding logic that must not change; and the team tracks token cost per engineer. The goals are to help engineers understand legacy systems quickly, produce convention-compliant boilerplate, and automate repetitive chores without surprising anyone."},{"domain":3,"stem":"A new Tollgate step was added to summarize failing integration tests. The step never errors, yet every run consumes the full 45-minute job ceiling before being killed, and the job log shows only Claude Code's startup banner. The step is:\n\n- run: claude \"Summarize the failures in test-output.log and suggest a likely root cause\" --allowedTools \"Read,Grep\"\n\nWhat is the most likely root cause?","options":["The command omits the `-p` (print) flag, so Claude Code starts an interactive session and waits indefinitely for terminal input that the unattended runner can never provide.","The `--allowedTools` list excludes Bash, so Claude Code cannot run the test suite itself and keeps retrying the denied tool call until the runner's global timeout kills it.","The command omits `--output-format json`, so Claude Code buffers its free-text answer in memory and never flushes the summary to stdout before the job ceiling is reached.","The command lacks a `--max-turns` limit, so the agentic loop keeps calling Read and Grep on the log file without converging, exhausting the runner's time without producing any output."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Claude Code의 기본 동작은 interactive(REPL) 세션입니다. `-p`(print mode) 없이 실행하면 세션을 연 뒤 사용자 입력을 기다리는데, 터미널이 없는 CI 러너에서는 그 입력이 영원히 오지 않으므로 job이 hang되어 전역 timeout까지 러너 시간만 소모합니다. 로그에 시작 배너만 있고 아무 도구 호출 흔적도 없다는 점이 \"작업을 시작조차 하지 않았다\"는 결정적 증거입니다. 이런 hang은 시끄럽게 실패하지 않는다는 점이 특징이며, 거의 항상 플래그 하나 누락이 원인입니다. 수정은 `claude -p \"...\"`로 바꾸고 step timeout도 함께 두는 것입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 자동화·CI 시나리오 → 반드시 non-interactive `-p`; 누락 시 조용한 hang — Task Statement 3.6 · 출처: Section 12 (L82)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 허용되지 않은 도구는 거부될 뿐이고, 요약 작업에는 Read/Grep으로 충분합니다. 로그에 도구 호출 자체가 없으므로 원인이 아닙니다.\n- C: `--output-format json`은 파싱 편의를 위한 동반 플래그일 뿐, 없다고 출력이 멈추지 않습니다(기본 text로 stdout 출력).\n- D: `--max-turns`는 runaway 방지에 유용하지만, 이 job은 루프를 돌기 전 입력 대기 상태에 머물러 있어 다른 근본 원인을 고치는 선택지입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"에러 없이 timeout까지 멈춤 + 시작 배너만\"이면 `-p` 누락을 먼저 의심하세요.","id":"scenario-b-16","task":"3.6","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Senior engineer Priya wrote Harbor Ledger's review rules (\"flag any monetary arithmetic using floating point\", \"require idempotency keys on payment endpoints\") and Claude Code follows them perfectly when she reviews code on her laptop. Tollgate's PR reviews on GitHub Actions ignore these rules entirely, and so do sessions run by two newly hired engineers. Nothing errors or warns. Where did Priya most likely place the rules, and what should the team do?","options":["In `.claude/settings.json` under a custom `reviewRules` key; the team should move them into `.claude/settings.local.json`, which Claude Code reads on every runner and every engineer's machine.","In her user-level `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`; the team should move them into the project's root `CLAUDE.md` and commit it, so every checkout, including the CI runner, loads them.","In a `CLAUDE.local.md` at the repository root; the team should add a CI step that copies her file onto each runner before Claude Code starts, preserving her single source of truth.","In a subdirectory `CLAUDE.md` under `payments/`; the team should duplicate the same rules into every other subdirectory so that the reviewer sees them regardless of which files a PR touches."],"answer":1,"explanation":"본인 머신에서만 동작하고 CI와 신규 입사자에게는 적용되지 않는 패턴은 팀 표준이 user-level `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`에 들어 있다는 전형적인 신호입니다. user 파일은 그 사람의 홈 디렉터리에만 있으므로 저장소를 체크아웃한 러너나 다른 사람에게 전달되지 않고, 오류나 경고도 없는 silent failure가 됩니다. 배치 기준은 \"이 지시가 누구를 위한 것인가\"이며, 팀 전체가 따라야 하는 규칙은 project `CLAUDE.md`에 두고 반드시 커밋해야 합니다. 그러면 체크아웃만으로 Tollgate와 모든 엔지니어가 같은 규칙을 로드합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 팀 표준을 user config에 두면 silent failure → 커밋된 project CLAUDE.md로 이동 — Task Statement 3.1 · 출처: Section 10 (L63, L64)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: settings.json에는 지시문용 `reviewRules` 같은 키가 없고, `settings.local.json`은 커밋되지 않는 개인 설정이라 오히려 공유가 안 됩니다.\n- C: `CLAUDE.local.md`는 git-ignored 개인용 파일입니다. 러너에 복사하는 우회는 팀원 세션 문제를 해결하지 못하고 잘못된 위치를 고착시킵니다.\n- D: 하위 디렉터리 CLAUDE.md도 커밋되면 공유되므로 \"Priya만 동작\"하는 증상과 맞지 않으며, 복제는 drift를 낳습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"나만 되고 CI·동료는 안 됨, 경고 없음\" → user-level에 둔 팀 규칙입니다.","id":"scenario-b-17","task":"3.1","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":4,"stem":"Tollgate's review prompt currently says: \"Review this diff thoroughly and report anything that could be a problem. Be careful and only flag real issues.\" Developers report that roughly 60% of comments are noise: naming preferences, speculative \"might be slow\" remarks, and complaints about code the PR did not change. Leadership wants false positives halved without losing genuine defect reports. What is the most effective first change?","options":["Ask Claude to attach a self-assessed confidence score from 1 to 10 to every finding, and have the posting script suppress any comment whose score is below 7 before it reaches the PR.","Strengthen the existing wording to \"Be extremely conservative; when in doubt, do not comment,\" and move that sentence to the very top of the prompt so it carries more weight.","Define explicit reporting criteria: which defect categories to report, which to skip (style, untouched lines), and what concrete evidence each finding must cite from the changed code.","Add a second Claude pass that re-reads every posted comment and deletes those it judges to be noise, leaving the original broad review prompt unchanged to preserve recall."],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"철저히 검토하라\", \"진짜 문제만 표시하라\"는 무엇이 문제인지 정의하지 않는 모호한 지시이므로 모델이 스스로 기준을 추측하게 되고, 그 결과가 스타일 지적과 추측성 코멘트입니다. 오탐을 줄이는 가장 효과적인 첫 수는 explicit criteria, 즉 보고할 결함 범주(예: 금액 연산 오류, 누락된 오류 처리), 보고하지 않을 범주(스타일, 변경되지 않은 줄), 그리고 각 finding이 변경된 코드에서 인용해야 할 구체적 근거를 명시하는 것입니다. 기준이 명확하면 precision이 오르면서도 정의된 결함 범주의 recall은 유지됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 오탐 감소는 \"조심하라\"가 아니라 보고/비보고 기준의 명시로 — Task Statement 4.1 · 출처: Section 13 (L83, L84)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 모델의 자기 평가 confidence는 보정(calibration)이 되어 있지 않아 신뢰할 수 있는 필터가 아니며, 기준 자체가 모호한 문제를 고치지 않습니다.\n- B: \"더 보수적으로\"는 여전히 모호한 지시라 진짜 결함까지 같이 누락시키거나 효과가 일관되지 않습니다.\n- D: 약한 주 프롬프트를 리뷰 패스로 땜질하는 안티패턴입니다. 비용·지연만 늘고 근본 원인은 남습니다(프롬프트를 먼저 고친 뒤 검토 층 추가).\n\n시험 팁: 오탐 문제의 첫 수는 거의 항상 \"무엇을 보고하고 무엇을 건너뛸지\"를 명시하는 것입니다.","id":"scenario-b-18","task":"4.1","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Harbor Ledger's test conventions (use the shared `fakeClock` fixture, never hit the real ledger database, name tests `should_<behavior>`) apply to every `*.test.ts` and `*_test.go` file. These test files sit next to the code they cover in more than 60 different packages. The root `CLAUDE.md` is already 380 lines, and Tollgate's test-generation job often ignores rules buried in it. How should the team deliver the test conventions?","options":["Place a `CLAUDE.md` with the test conventions in each of the 60 package directories, so the rules lazily load whenever Claude reads any file in a package that contains tests.","Package the conventions as a skill under `.claude/skills/test-conventions/` with a detailed description, so Claude loads them on demand whenever it decides a task involves testing.","Create `.claude/rules/testing.md` with a `paths` frontmatter listing `**/*.test.ts` and `**/*_test.go`, so the rules load only when Claude actually reads a matching test file in any package.","Move the conventions to the top of the root `CLAUDE.md` and mark them with \"IMPORTANT\" so they are seen first, then trim other sections until the file is under 400 lines."],"answer":2,"explanation":"이 관례는 특정 폴더가 아니라 파일 유형을 따르며, 테스트 파일이 60개 이상의 패키지에 흩어져 있습니다. 이런 경우의 정답 도구는 `.claude/rules/`의 path-scoped rule입니다. `paths` frontmatter에 glob을 지정하면 규칙은 시작 시 로드되지 않고 일치하는 파일을 Claude가 읽을 때만 로드되므로, 이미 비대한 always-on 컨텍스트를 늘리지 않으면서 필요한 순간에 정확히 적용됩니다. 원칙은 \"Convention follows the folder → subdirectory CLAUDE.md, follows the file type → rule\"입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 폴더를 가로지르는 파일 유형별 관례 = `paths` glob이 있는 rule — Task Statement 3.3 · 출처: Section 10 (L67)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 60개 파일 복제는 drift를 낳고, 패키지의 테스트 외 파일을 읽어도 로드되어 범위도 부정확합니다. 폴더 기반 관례에 맞는 도구입니다.\n- B: Skill은 가끔 실행하는 다단계 절차용이며 description 매칭에 의존하므로, 테스트 파일을 만질 때마다 지켜야 하는 상시 관례를 보장하지 못합니다.\n- D: 이미 약 200줄을 넘어 준수율이 떨어진 상태에서 always-on 파일에 계속 의존하는 것은 근본 문제(컨텍스트 비대)를 해결하지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"흩어진 테스트 파일\"은 path-scoped rule의 대표 사례입니다.","id":"scenario-b-19","task":"3.3","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":4,"stem":"After Claude Code finishes a review, a Tollgate step sends its prose summary to the Messages API with the instruction \"Return a JSON array of findings with file, line, severity, and message.\" About 4% of responses break the comment-posting script: some wrap the array in Markdown fences, some add a leading sentence, and a few use `sev` instead of `severity`. What is the most reliable fix?","options":["Add three few-shot examples of correctly formatted arrays to the instruction, and have the posting script strip Markdown fences and leading text with a regular expression before parsing.","Define a `report_findings` tool whose `input_schema` specifies the required fields and types, and set `tool_choice` to force that tool so the findings arrive as structured tool input.","Lower the temperature to 0 so the model produces the same format every time, and add a retry that re-sends the request whenever the posting script throws a JSON parse error.","Prefill the assistant turn with an opening bracket, and add \"Respond ONLY with valid JSON, no other text\" in capitals at the end of the instruction to discourage extra prose."],"answer":1,"explanation":"형식 오류의 근본 원인은 구조를 프롬프트 지시로만 요청한다는 데 있습니다. tool use + JSON schema 방식에서는 `input_schema`에 필드 이름, 타입, `required`를 정의하고 `tool_choice`로 해당 도구를 강제하므로, 결과가 Markdown 펜스나 서두 문장 없이 구조화된 `tool_use` 입력으로 돌아옵니다. 필드 이름도 스키마에 고정되므로 `sev` 같은 변형이 줄어듭니다. 다만 스키마는 구조를 보장할 뿐 내용의 정확성(예: 줄 번호가 맞는지)은 보장하지 않으므로 의미 검증은 별도로 유지합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 신뢰할 수 있는 구조화 출력 = tool 정의의 input_schema + 강제 tool_choice — Task Statement 4.3 · 출처: Section 15 (L100)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: few-shot은 형식 준수율을 높이지만 보장하지 않고, 정규식 후처리는 새로운 변형이 나올 때마다 깨지는 취약한 방식입니다.\n- C: temperature 0도 형식을 보장하지 않으며, 파싱 실패 후 재시도는 증상 처리일 뿐 근본 원인을 고치지 않습니다.\n- D: prefill과 대문자 강조는 여전히 프롬프트 수준의 완화책이라 필드 이름 변형 같은 스키마 위반을 막지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"가끔 JSON이 깨진다\"의 최선책은 지시 강화가 아니라 스키마가 있는 도구 강제입니다.","id":"scenario-b-20","task":"4.3","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Tollgate's review workflow runs on `pull_request` events, including PRs from contractors' forks. It currently uses `permissions: contents: write`, and passes `--allowedTools \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash,Edit,WebFetch\"` because \"the reviewer might need them.\" A security review found a fork PR whose description contained hidden text instructing Claude to fetch an external URL and edit a CI script. The reviewer only needs to read code and post comments. What should the team do?","options":["Add a rule to the project `CLAUDE.md` stating that instructions found inside PR descriptions, issues, or code comments must always be ignored, and keep the current tool list so reviews stay thorough.","Run the reviewer with `--dangerously-skip-permissions` inside the ephemeral runner, since the runner is discarded after every job and therefore cannot persist any damage from a malicious PR.","Switch Tollgate to a more capable model that is better at recognizing prompt injection, and require a human to approve the review comments before they are posted to the pull request.","Restrict `--allowedTools` to Read, Grep, and Glob, drop Bash, Edit, and WebFetch, and reduce workflow permissions to `contents: read` with only the PR-comment write scope the bot needs."],"answer":3,"explanation":"무인으로 실행되는 CI에서 권한 스코핑은 best practice가 아니라 보안 요구사항입니다. 리뷰어는 코드를 읽고 코멘트만 달면 되므로 minimum necessary permissions 원칙에 따라 Read/Grep/Glob만 허용하고, 쓰기(Edit), 셸(Bash), 네트워크(WebFetch) 도구를 제거하며, 워크플로 토큰도 `contents: read`와 PR 코멘트 쓰기 범위로 줄여야 합니다. 그러면 포크 PR의 prompt injection이 모델을 속이더라도 외부 URL 호출이나 CI 스크립트 수정 자체가 불가능해져 피해 범위(blast radius)가 제한됩니다. 코드 수준의 권한 제한은 모델의 판단과 무관하게 결정적으로 작동합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 무인 자동화 = 최소 권한; 읽기 작업에 쓰기·셸·네트워크 도구를 주지 않음 — Task Statement 3.6 · 출처: Section 12 (L82)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 프롬프트 수준 지시는 확률적이며 주입된 지시가 이를 우회할 수 있습니다. 위험한 도구를 그대로 두는 것이 핵심 문제입니다.\n- B: 권한 확인 전체를 끄는 것은 정반대 방향입니다. 러너가 일회용이어도 네트워크 유출과 secret 노출은 job 중에 일어납니다.\n- C: 더 강한 모델도 injection을 확실히 막지 못하며, 사람 승인은 코멘트만 다룰 뿐 실행 중 fetch·edit를 막지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: 포크 PR + 넓은 도구 = 정답은 거의 항상 도구와 토큰 권한의 최소화입니다.","id":"scenario-b-21","task":"3.6","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Tollgate's nightly flaky-test job uses the Agent SDK. Its first phase spends about 40 turns exploring the test harness and ends with a detailed diagnosis; the session ID is saved. The team now wants two remediation strategies, \"add retries with jitter\" and \"replace the shared clock fixture,\" to be attempted in parallel in separate checkouts, each starting from the full diagnosis context without either attempt's history leaking into the other. How should the two attempts be started?","options":["Start both attempts with `continue_conversation=True` so each picks up the most recent session automatically, and pass the strategy name in each follow-up prompt.","Start each attempt with `resume=<saved session ID>` and `fork_session=True`, so each branches into its own new session that inherits the diagnosis while the original stays intact.","Start each attempt with `resume=<saved session ID>` only, so both continue the diagnosis session directly and the full history of the shared investigation remains in one place.","Start two fresh sessions with `query()` and paste the diagnosis text into each prompt, since resumed sessions cannot run concurrently and forking is limited to the interactive CLI."],"answer":1,"explanation":"요구사항은 \"같은 출발점(진단 완료 시점)에서 두 대안을 서로 오염 없이 시도\"하는 것이며, 이는 정확히 fork의 용도입니다. `resume=session_id`에 `fork_session=True`를 함께 주면 그 시점의 대화 상태를 물려받은 새 session ID로 분기하고 원본 세션은 그대로 남으므로, 두 시도가 각자의 기록을 따로 쌓습니다. 40턴의 비싼 탐색을 반복하지 않고도 전체 진단 컨텍스트를 유지할 수 있습니다. 참고로 세션 분기는 대화 상태만 복원하며 파일 변경은 분리하지 않으므로, 문제에서처럼 별도 체크아웃을 쓰는 것이 맞습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: resume = 같은 세션 이어감, fork_session = 새 ID로 분기(원본 보존), continue = 가장 최근 세션 — Task Statement 1.7 · 출처: Section 12 (L81, S2)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: continue는 \"가장 최근\" 세션에 의존하므로 병렬 실행에서는 어떤 세션을 잡을지 불확실하고, 두 시도가 같은 세션을 공유하게 됩니다.\n- C: 둘 다 같은 세션 ID를 그대로 이어가면 두 시도의 기록이 같은 세션에 섞여 서로의 맥락을 오염시킵니다.\n- D: 진단을 텍스트로 붙여 넣으면 40턴 동안 쌓인 도구 결과와 맥락이 손실되며, fork가 CLI 전용이라는 전제도 틀립니다(SDK가 지원).\n\n시험 팁: \"같은 출발점에서 두 대안\" = fork_session입니다.","id":"scenario-b-22","task":"1.7","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Tollgate supports a `/tollgate fix` comment that lets Claude push commits to a PR. It works well for one-line lint fixes. Last week a developer used it on a PR requesting \"migrate all services to the new error envelope,\" and Claude edited 23 files across 9 services in a way the owning teams rejected, forcing a painful revert. The platform team wants large, cross-service changes reviewed before any file is touched, without slowing the lint-fix path. What is the best design?","options":["Keep direct execution for every request but require that Claude open a separate draft PR instead of pushing to the original branch, so reviewers can reject unwanted edits before merging them.","Run every `/tollgate fix` request in plan mode first, including lint fixes, so a written plan is always posted and approved by a human before any commit is pushed to the branch.","Route multi-module or contract-changing requests through a plan-mode run that posts its plan for approval, then execute the approved plan; keep direct execution for small mechanical fixes.","Add a sentence to the fix prompt telling Claude to describe its intended changes and wait for confirmation before editing files whenever a request appears to span several services."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Plan mode는 승인 전에는 파일을 쓰지 않는 read-only permission mode이므로, 여러 모듈에 걸치거나 API/스키마 계약을 바꾸는 변경처럼 되돌리기 어렵고 범위가 큰 작업에 적합합니다. 계획(순서 있는 단계, 수정할 파일, 위험)을 게시해 소유 팀이 범위를 검토·수정한 뒤 실행하면 23개 파일 revert 같은 사고를 예방할 수 있습니다. 반면 단일 파일의 기계적 수정에는 plan이 오버헤드일 뿐이므로 direct execution을 유지하는 것이 요구사항(\"lint 경로를 늦추지 말 것\")에 맞습니다. 판단 기준은 되돌리기 난이도와 다중 모듈 여부입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 큰 cross-module 변경 = plan 먼저(권한 경계), 작은 기계적 수정 = direct — Task Statement 3.4 · 출처: Section 11 (L78, L79)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 별도 PR은 사후 검토일 뿐 잘못된 방향으로 작업이 이미 수행된 뒤라 낭비가 크고, 사전 합의라는 요구를 충족하지 못합니다.\n- B: 모든 lint 수정에도 plan을 강제하면 요구사항이 금지한 지연이 생깁니다(과잉 설계).\n- D: 프롬프트 지시는 보장이 없고, 무인 실행에서 \"확인을 기다려라\"는 의미가 없습니다. plan mode는 예의가 아니라 권한 경계입니다.\n\n시험 팁: Plan mode의 판단 기준은 \"몇 개 모듈인가, 되돌리기 어려운가\"입니다.","id":"scenario-b-23","task":"3.4","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":4,"stem":"Tollgate makes two kinds of Claude calls: (1) the PR review, which is a required status check that blocks merging, and (2) the nightly audit, which asks a single-turn question (\"list untested branches in this file\") for each of roughly 6,000 source files and whose results are read the next morning. Finance asks the team to cut API costs using the Message Batches API. What is the best plan?","options":["Move both workloads to the Batches API to capture the 50% discount everywhere, and raise the PR status check timeout so that merges simply wait for the batch results to arrive.","Move the nightly audit to the Batches API and read the results back in submission order, since each line of the results file corresponds to the file at the same position in the request list.","Move the PR review to the Batches API because each review needs several tool round-trips, and keep the nightly audit synchronous because its 6,000 requests exceed the batch size limit.","Move only the nightly audit to the Batches API, tag each request with a `custom_id` naming its source file, match results by that ID, and keep the merge-gating PR review synchronous."],"answer":3,"explanation":"배치 적합성의 판단 질문은 \"이것이 도는 동안 막혀 있는 것이 있는가?\"입니다. Message Batches API는 같은 모델·같은 품질로 50% 할인을 주지만 처리 상한이 24시간이고 지연 보장이 없으므로, merge를 막는 gating 체크에는 쓰면 안 되고, 다음 날 아침에 읽는 야간 감사에는 이상적입니다. 결과는 완료 순서로 오므로 각 요청에 원본 파일을 가리키는 `custom_id`를 붙이고 그 ID로 매칭해야 하며, 위치로 읽으면 오류 없이 엉뚱한 파일에 결과가 붙습니다. 6,000건은 100,000건 한도 안이고, 감사는 single-turn이라 배치에 맞습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 지연 허용 작업만 배치, gating 체크는 동기; 결과는 custom_id로 상관 — Task Statement 4.5 · 출처: Section 15 (L106)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 24시간 상한은 merge 차단 체크에게 할인이 아니라 예약된 장애입니다.\n- B: 대상 선택은 맞지만 결과를 제출 순서로 읽는 것은 대표적 함정입니다. 결과 순서는 보장되지 않습니다.\n- C: 배치 요청은 중간에 도구를 실행해 결과를 되먹이는 왕복이 불가하므로 다단계 도구 루프에 맞지 않고, 6,000건은 한도 이내입니다.\n\n시험 팁: Batches 문제는 \"누가 기다리나\"와 \"custom_id 매칭\" 두 가지를 확인하세요.","id":"scenario-b-24","task":"4.5","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"The team created a skill at `.claude/skills/release-notes/SKILL.md` that drafts release notes from merged PRs and writes them to `CHANGELOG.md`. Its description reads \"Helps summarize code changes.\" During ordinary Tollgate review runs, Claude has started invoking the skill on its own and appending changelog entries to contributors' branches. The team wants the skill to run only when someone explicitly types `/release-notes`. What is the best fix?","options":["Add `allowed-tools: Read` to the skill's frontmatter so that, whenever Claude invokes the skill automatically, it can no longer write to `CHANGELOG.md` on a contributor's branch.","Add `trigger: manual` and `version: 2` to the skill's frontmatter so that Claude Code registers the updated skill as a command-only skill and stops matching it during reviews.","Add `disable-model-invocation: true` to the skill's frontmatter so Claude never invokes it automatically on its own, while `/release-notes` typed by a user still runs it directly.","Move the release-notes procedure into the project `CLAUDE.md` under a heading that tells Claude to run it only when the user explicitly asks for release notes to be generated."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Skill은 description 매칭으로 Claude가 자동 호출할 수 있으며, \"Helps summarize code changes\"처럼 넓은 설명은 리뷰 작업과도 매칭되어 의도치 않은 자동 실행을 낳습니다. 사용자가 명시적으로 호출할 때만 실행되게 하는 정확한 장치는 frontmatter의 `disable-model-invocation: true`입니다. 이렇게 하면 모델의 자동 호출은 막히고, 폴더 이름(`/release-notes`)을 통한 direct invocation은 그대로 동작합니다. description을 더 구체적으로 다듬는 것도 도움이 되지만, \"명시 호출만\"이라는 요구를 보장하는 것은 이 필드입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: manual-only skill = `disable-model-invocation: true` — Task Statement 3.2 · 출처: Section 11 (L73, L74)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: `allowed-tools`는 권한을 사전 승인하는 필드이지 도구를 제한하는 필드가 아니며, 자동 호출 자체도 막지 못합니다.\n- B: `trigger`, `version`은 존재하지 않는 frontmatter 필드입니다. 무시될 뿐 동작이 바뀌지 않습니다.\n- D: CLAUDE.md는 매 세션 항상 로드되는 상시 지시용이라 가끔 쓰는 다단계 절차에 맞지 않고, 실행 조건도 확률적 지시에 의존합니다.\n\n시험 팁: 존재하지 않는 frontmatter 필드(trigger, version)를 고르는 함정에 주의하세요.","id":"scenario-b-25","task":"3.2","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":4,"stem":"For a 38-file PR that renamed a currency-rounding helper and updated its callers, Tollgate's single review pass produced detailed comments on the first dozen files, generic remarks on the rest, and missed that two services now round in opposite directions. Re-running the same pass gave a different set of comments each time. What is the best way to restructure the review?","options":["Review each changed file in its own focused pass for local defects, then run a separate integration pass that receives the per-file summaries and checks cross-file consistency such as rounding behavior.","Switch the single pass to a model with a larger context window so all 38 files fit with room to spare, and instruct it to give every file equal attention before writing any comments.","Run the same single-pass review three times on the whole PR and post only the findings that appear in at least two of the three runs, discarding the rest as inconsistent noise.","Ask the developer to split the PR into several PRs of at most five files each, so that every PR fits comfortably within a single review pass with consistent attention throughout."],"answer":0,"explanation":"앞쪽 파일만 자세하고 뒤로 갈수록 일반적인 코멘트가 나오는 것은 큰 입력에서의 attention dilution 증상이며, 실행마다 결과가 달라지는 것도 같은 원인에서 옵니다. 해결책은 multi-pass review로 구조를 바꾸는 것입니다. 파일별로 집중된 패스에서 국소 결함을 찾고, 별도의 integration pass가 파일별 요약을 받아 \"두 서비스의 반올림 방향 불일치\" 같은 cross-file 문제를 점검합니다. 각 패스의 범위가 좁고 기준이 명확해 결과가 일관되고, 파일 간 상호작용도 전담 패스에서 다뤄집니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 큰 리뷰 = 파일별 local pass + 별도 cross-file integration pass — Task Statement 4.6 · 출처: Section 15 (L103)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 컨텍스트 창이 커도 주의 분산 문제는 남으며, \"골고루 보라\"는 지시만으로 해결되지 않습니다.\n- C: 같은 구조를 반복하면 같은 사각지대가 반복되고, 다수결은 놓친 cross-file 결함을 새로 찾아내지 못합니다.\n- D: 리뷰 시스템의 한계를 개발자에게 떠넘기며, PR을 나누면 파일 간 일관성 문제를 오히려 보기 어려워집니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"앞부분만 자세함 + cross-file 결함 누락\"이면 per-file + integration 구조가 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-26","task":"4.6","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Tollgate's review step runs `claude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format json --max-turns 12` and pipes the output into the comment script. Last night a review of a large PR posted \"No issues found\" and the status check went green, although the PR contained an obvious SQL injection. The saved JSON shows `\"subtype\": \"error_max_turns\"` and a `result` holding a partial sentence. The comment script treats any parseable output as a completed review. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Raise `--max-turns` to 50 for all reviews so large PRs can finish, and keep the comment script unchanged because it already handles every JSON response that Claude Code returns.","Switch to `--output-format stream-json` so the comment script can watch events as they arrive and post findings incrementally before the run reaches its turn limit.","Add a line to the review prompt telling Claude to always output \"REVIEW INCOMPLETE\" when it runs short of turns, and have the comment script search for that phrase first.","Make the step check the exit code and the result's `subtype` and `is_error` fields, validate the findings shape, and fail the status check for any run that did not complete successfully."],"answer":3,"explanation":"근본 원인은 파이프라인이 결과를 검증하지 않고 \"파싱되면 성공\"으로 간주한 데 있습니다. headless 출력 처리의 원칙은 exit code 확인, 구조화 결과가 항상 정상이라고 가정하지 않기, 그리고 하류에서 쓰기 전에 shape 검증입니다. `--output-format json` 결과에는 `subtype`(예: `success`, `error_max_turns`)과 `is_error`가 있으므로, 성공으로 완료되지 않은 실행은 status check를 실패로 처리해야 합니다. 그래야 불완전한 리뷰가 \"문제 없음\"으로 둔갑해 머지를 통과시키는 silent failure가 사라집니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: CI step은 exit code·subtype·shape를 검증하고 불완전 실행은 실패 처리 — Task Statement 3.6 · 출처: Section 12 (L82, S3)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 턴 상한을 올려도 언젠가 다시 한도에 걸리며, 검증 없는 스크립트라는 근본 원인이 남습니다. 상한 자체는 runaway 방지에 필요합니다.\n- B: stream-json은 실시간 진행 표시용입니다. 부분 결과를 게시하면 불완전한 리뷰가 오히려 더 빨리 확정됩니다.\n- C: 턴 한도 도달은 모델이 제어하는 상황이 아니므로 프롬프트 지시로 표시를 보장할 수 없습니다. 결정적 필드를 써야 합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"파싱되면 성공\"은 CI의 대표적 silent failure입니다. subtype/is_error/exit code를 확인하세요.","id":"scenario-b-27","task":"3.6","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"An engineer is using Claude Code to write `normalizeAmount()`, which Tollgate will later use to compare currency values in review findings. The spec is a paragraph of prose (\"handle locales sensibly, round like the ledger does\"). After four rounds of \"that's still not quite right,\" the function still mishandles inputs such as `\"1.234,50\"` and `\"-0.005\"`. What should the engineer do next to converge fastest?","options":["Give Claude a concrete set of input/expected-output cases, have it write them as tests first, then implement and iterate by running the tests and feeding back the specific failures.","Rewrite the prose specification in much greater detail, covering every locale and rounding rule in full sentences, and ask Claude to regenerate the function from scratch.","Switch to plan mode and ask Claude to produce a step-by-step plan for the function, then approve it and let Claude implement the plan without further feedback.","Clear the conversation with `/clear`, start a fresh session, and paste the same prose specification again so that Claude is not anchored by its earlier attempts."],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"아직 아니다\"를 반복하는 피드백은 무엇이 틀렸는지 알려 주지 않으므로 수렴이 느립니다. Iterative refinement를 가장 빠르게 수렴시키는 방법은 모호한 산문 대신 구체적인 입력/기대 출력 예시를 주고, 이를 테스트로 먼저 작성(test-driven)하게 한 뒤, 구현하고 테스트를 실행해 구체적인 실패 내용을 다시 피드백하는 루프입니다. 예시는 \"sensibly\", \"like the ledger does\" 같은 표현의 모호성을 제거하고, 테스트는 매 반복마다 객관적인 검증 기준을 제공합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 모호한 요구는 구체적 예시 → 테스트 먼저 → 실패 피드백 반복으로 수렴 — Task Statement 3.5 · 출처: Section 11 (L79), Section 14 (L95)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 더 긴 산문도 여전히 해석의 여지를 남기며, 검증 가능한 기준(테스트)이 없어 같은 문제가 반복됩니다.\n- C: Plan mode는 다중 파일·고위험 변경의 사전 합의용입니다. 단일 함수의 동작 정의 문제를 해결하지 못하고 피드백 루프도 없앱니다.\n- D: 같은 모호한 스펙을 다시 주면 같은 결과가 나옵니다. 컨텍스트 초기화가 아닌 입력의 구체성이 문제입니다.\n\n시험 팁: 반복해도 안 맞을 때는 \"구체적 예시 + 테스트 + 실패 피드백\"이 정석입니다.","id":"scenario-b-28","task":"3.5","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Harbor Ledger's review standards are written out in full in three places: the root `CLAUDE.md`, the `.claude/commands/review-pr.md` command that engineers run locally, and the prompt string in Tollgate's workflow YAML. Over three months the copies drifted, and local reviews now disagree with Tollgate's on whether unchecked `parseInt` results are a defect. What is the best way to reorganize this?","options":["Keep all three copies but add a CI job that diffs them on every commit and fails the build whenever the three versions of the review standards are not textually identical.","Move the standards into each engineer's `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` so they apply in every project, and delete the copies from the repository and from Tollgate's workflow YAML entirely.","Keep the standards in one committed file such as `docs/review-standards.md`, import it from `CLAUDE.md` with `@docs/review-standards.md`, and have the command and workflow prompt reference it, not copy it.","Keep the standards only in the workflow YAML prompt, since CI is the authoritative reviewer, and tell engineers to copy that prompt whenever they want to run an equivalent local review."],"answer":2,"explanation":"같은 지시를 여러 곳에 복제하면 drift가 생긴다는 것이 문제의 근본 원인이며, slash command가 CLAUDE.md 지시를 복제하는 것도 대표적 안티패턴입니다. 해결책은 single source of truth를 두고 나머지가 이를 참조하게 하는 모듈식 구성입니다. CLAUDE.md는 `@path` import로 다른 파일을 가져올 수 있으므로, 표준을 커밋된 한 파일에 두고 CLAUDE.md에서 import하면 로컬 세션과 Tollgate 모두 같은 내용을 로드합니다. command와 워크플로 프롬프트는 표준을 다시 쓰지 않고 그 파일을 따르도록 지시하면 됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 지시 복제 = drift; 한 파일 + `@import`로 모듈화하고 참조 — Task Statement 3.1 · 출처: Section 10 (L68, L69, S2), Section 11 (L72)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 일치 검사는 증상을 감지할 뿐 세 곳을 수동으로 동시에 고치는 부담을 남기는 과잉 설계입니다.\n- B: 팀 표준을 user-level에 두면 CI 러너와 신규 인원에게 전달되지 않는 silent failure가 됩니다.\n- D: 로컬에서 수동 복사에 의존하면 같은 drift가 다시 생기고, 인터랙티브 세션에는 표준이 자동으로 로드되지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"여러 곳의 복사본이 어긋났다\"는 하나의 원본 + import/참조로 해결합니다.","id":"scenario-b-29","task":"3.1","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":3,"stem":"When GitHub's API briefly returns errors, the Actions runner retries Tollgate's review step. After such incidents, PRs show two or three identical sets of review comments, and the auto-generated `TESTS_ADDED.md` contains duplicated entries. A teammate proposes passing `--continue` so the retried run \"remembers\" what it already posted. What should the team do instead?","options":["Disable automatic retries for the review step entirely, so that a transient GitHub API error fails the job and a developer must re-run the workflow manually after checking the PR.","Adopt `--continue` as proposed, because the retried run will resume the previous session on the runner and can therefore see which comments and entries were already written.","Add an instruction to the review prompt telling Claude not to post a comment or add an entry if it believes the same content was already written earlier in the pipeline.","Make the step idempotent: tag Tollgate's comments with a marker and update rather than re-create them, and have the file step check for existing entries before writing."],"answer":3,"explanation":"CI 파이프라인은 실패 시 재시도하므로, 자동화 작업은 두 번 실행해도 결과가 같은 idempotent 설계여야 합니다. 마커로 Tollgate 코멘트를 식별해 이미 있으면 갱신(update)하고, 파일 쓰기 전에 기존 항목을 확인하면 재시도 횟수와 무관하게 결과가 한 번만 반영됩니다. 또한 각 호출은 이전 실행을 기억하지 않는다는 전제로 self-contained하게 설계해야 하므로, \"이전 세션 기억\"에 의존하는 `--continue`는 해법이 아닙니다. 에피메랄 러너에서는 재시도된 job이 이전 세션 파일조차 갖고 있지 않을 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 자동화 작업 4원칙 중 idempotent + self-contained — Task Statement 3.6 · 출처: Section 12 (L82)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 재시도는 일시적 오류에 대한 정당한 복원력입니다. 이를 끄면 다른 문제(수동 개입 증가)를 만들 뿐 중복의 근본 원인을 고치지 않습니다.\n- B: `--continue`는 가장 최근 세션에 의존하며, 새 러너에서는 그 세션이 없을 수 있고 외부 상태(코멘트)의 중복을 결정적으로 막지 못합니다.\n- C: 프롬프트 지시는 확률적이고, Claude가 이미 게시된 코멘트를 확인한다는 보장이 없습니다. 중복 방지는 코드로 강제해야 합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"재시도 후 중복\"이 나오면 정답은 idempotent 설계입니다.","id":"scenario-b-30","task":"3.6","scenario":"Claude Code for Continuous Integration","scenarioIntro":"Harbor Ledger is a payments company whose 140 engineers work in a single TypeScript/Go monorepo hosted on GitHub. The platform team runs \"Tollgate,\" a set of GitHub Actions workflows that invoke Claude Code on every pull request to post review findings, generate missing unit tests, and suggest fixes for failing builds. Tollgate jobs run on ephemeral Linux runners with a 45-minute job ceiling, and the Anthropic API key is stored as a repository secret. Review findings are posted as inline PR comments by a small Node script that parses Claude Code's output, so the output format must be machine-readable and stable. Team-wide coding and review standards live in the repository, while individual engineers also keep personal Claude Code configuration on their laptops. A nightly workflow audits the entire repository for untested code paths, and its results are only needed by the next morning. Engineering leadership has set two goals for the quarter: cut the rate of false-positive review comments in half, because developers have started ignoring Tollgate, and keep unattended jobs tightly permissioned, because the repository accepts pull requests from external contractors' forks. All questions below refer to Tollgate."},{"domain":1,"stem":"A developer wrote WaveAssist's core loop against the Messages API as follows:\n\nwhile True:\n    resp = client.messages.create(model=MODEL, tools=TOOLS, messages=messages)\n    messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": resp.content})\n    if any(block.type == \"text\" for block in resp.content):\n        break                      # model has \"answered\"\n    results = run_tools(resp.content)\n    messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n\nIn production, about 1 in 6 conversations end with a message like \"Let me pull up your roaming records for March…\" and then nothing further happens. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Add a system-prompt rule telling Claude never to write explanatory text in the same response as a tool call, so that text only appears once the final answer is ready.","Drive the loop by `stop_reason`: keep iterating while it is `\"tool_use\"`, executing every tool_use block and returning the results, and stop only when it is `\"end_turn\"`.","Raise the loop's maximum iteration limit and add a retry that re-sends the last user message whenever the assistant reply is shorter than a minimum character count.","Set `tool_choice` to `{\"type\": \"any\"}` on every request so the model is always forced to call a tool, and treat the first response without a tool call as the answer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Claude는 한 응답 안에 text block과 tool_use block을 함께 낼 수 있습니다. 이 코드는 \"text가 있으면 끝\"으로 판단하기 때문에, 도구 호출 직전의 안내 문구(\"Let me pull up…\")만 보고 루프를 종료해 버립니다. 올바른 agentic loop는 응답 내용이 아니라 `stop_reason`으로 제어합니다. `stop_reason == \"tool_use\"`이면 모든 tool_use 블록을 실행하고 각 `tool_use_id`에 대응하는 tool_result를 다음 user 메시지로 돌려준 뒤 계속하고, `\"end_turn\"`일 때만 종료합니다. 이렇게 하면 중간 안내 문구가 있어도 조사가 끝까지 진행됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 루프 종료 조건은 텍스트 유무가 아니라 `stop_reason`(\"tool_use\" → 계속, \"end_turn\" → 종료) — Task Statement 1.1 · 출처: Section 2 (L4)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 결정론적 제어 흐름 버그를 prompt-only fix로 덮으려는 것입니다. 모델이 text와 tool_use를 함께 내는 것은 정상 동작이며, 지시를 어기는 경우가 남습니다.\n- C: 반복 한도는 원인이 아닙니다. 루프는 한도에 도달하기 전에 잘못된 조건으로 빠져나가고 있으며, 길이 기반 재시도는 근본 원인과 무관한 휴리스틱입니다.\n- D: `any`를 매 요청에 강제하면 모델이 최종 답변을 할 수 없게 되어 루프 종료가 더 꼬입니다. 강제 도구 호출은 특정 단계에만 쓰는 수단입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"텍스트가 나왔으니 끝\" 같은 내용 기반 종료 조건이 보이면 `stop_reason` 기반 루프가 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-31","task":"1.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A business customer spends 50 minutes with WaveAssist disputing charges across four monthly bills. To stay within the context budget, the harness replaces older turns with a running prose summary every 20 turns. Near the end, WaveAssist offers a credit for \"about €90 in roaming charges from early spring,\" while the customer had identified exactly €112.40 across invoice numbers INV-3381 and INV-3517, dated 4 and 18 March. What is the best design change?","options":["Increase the summarization interval to every 40 turns and instruct the summarizer to be more careful about preserving numbers, invoice references, and dates from the conversation.","Stop summarizing entirely and rely on the model's full context window, because modern context windows are large enough to hold any realistic support conversation.","Replace prose summaries with a summary written in bullet points, and have the coordinator re-read the complete bill statements from the billing tool before every reply it writes.","Keep a structured case-facts block (amounts, invoice IDs, dates, customer's stated ask) outside the summarized history and re-inject it verbatim into each request."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Progressive summarization은 정확한 금액, 날짜, 식별자처럼 \"작지만 결정적인\" 사실을 \"약 €90, 초봄\" 같은 모호한 표현으로 뭉개는 경향이 있습니다. 이런 transactional facts는 요약 대상에서 빼내어 구조화된 persistent case-facts block으로 따로 관리하고, 매 요청마다 그대로(verbatim) 프롬프트에 넣어야 합니다. 그러면 오래된 대화는 요약해도 크레딧 금액과 송장 번호는 손실 없이 유지됩니다. 고객이 처음 요청한 내용(customer's stated ask)도 함께 보존해야 대화 후반에 목표가 흐려지지 않습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 요약은 사실을 잃는다 → 결정적 사실은 요약 밖의 구조화된 fact block으로 보존 — Task Statement 5.1 · 출처: Section 16 (L109–L110)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 요약 빈도와 \"조심하라\"는 지시를 바꿔도 요약이 사실을 압축·손실하는 구조는 그대로입니다(prompt-only fix).\n- B: 컨텍스트를 무한히 키우는 접근은 비용·지연이 크고, 긴 컨텍스트 중간의 정보가 덜 주목되는 문제(lost in the middle)도 해결하지 못합니다.\n- C: 형식만 bullet으로 바꿔도 요약 손실은 남고, 매 응답마다 전체 청구서를 다시 읽으면 tool-output bloat로 컨텍스트가 더 빨리 찹니다.\n\n시험 팁: 금액·날짜·ID가 \"대략\"으로 바뀌었다면 정답은 요약 개선이 아니라 요약 밖의 persistent fact block입니다.","id":"scenario-b-32","task":"5.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":2,"stem":"Logs show that when customers ask \"why is my bill higher this month?\", WaveAssist calls `get_usage_records` about 40% of the time, gets raw call and data events, and then struggles to explain plan fee changes that only appear on the statement. The two tools are currently described as follows:\n\nget_bill_statement: \"Gets billing information for a customer.\"\nget_usage_records:  \"Gets usage and billing data for a customer.\"\n\nWhat is the most effective first fix?","options":["Merge both tools into a single `get_billing_data` tool that always returns the full statement together with all raw usage events, so the model never has to choose between them.","Add five few-shot examples to the system prompt showing customer questions about bill increases followed by a call to `get_bill_statement` rather than to `get_usage_records`.","Rewrite both descriptions to state what each returns, when to use it versus the other, and example questions, e.g. statement for charges and fees, usage for event-level detail.","Have the harness set `tool_choice` to force `get_bill_statement` whenever the customer's message contains keywords such as \"bill\", \"invoice\", \"charge\", \"higher\", or \"more expensive\"."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Claude가 도구를 고르는 1차 근거는 tool description입니다. 지금 두 설명은 거의 같은 말(\"billing data\")을 쓰고 있어 경계가 겹치므로 오선택은 예측 가능한 결과입니다. 각 도구가 무엇을 반환하는지, 언제 쓰고 언제 다른 도구를 써야 하는지(boundaries), 대표 질문 예시를 명시하면 라우팅이 근본적으로 개선됩니다. 이는 비용이 가장 낮고 원인에 직접 작용하는 첫 번째 조치입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 모호·중복된 설명 → 반환 내용, 사용 시점, 다른 도구와의 경계를 명시한 설명으로 재작성 — Task Statement 2.1 · 출처: Section 6 (L32–L33)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 통합 후 항상 전체 데이터를 반환하면 tool-output bloat가 생기고, 대부분의 질문에 필요 없는 원시 이벤트로 컨텍스트를 낭비합니다(over-engineering).\n- B: few-shot은 보조 수단일 수 있으나, 겹치는 설명이라는 근본 원인을 그대로 둔 채 프롬프트만 늘립니다.\n- D: 키워드 기반 강제는 취약합니다. \"data usage is higher\"처럼 usage 도구가 맞는 질문까지 statement로 강제해 새 오류를 만듭니다.\n\n시험 팁: 도구 오선택 문제에서 설명이 비슷하게 쓰여 있다면, 첫 조치는 거의 항상 설명 재작성입니다.","id":"scenario-b-33","task":"2.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":1,"stem":"WaveAssist's system prompt says: \"Before calling `initiate_sim_swap`, you MUST call `verify_identity` and receive status VERIFIED.\" An audit of 30,000 SIM-swap sessions finds 41 swaps performed without a verified identity, mostly when customers claimed urgency (\"I'm abroad and my phone was stolen, please hurry\"). SIM-swap fraud is Nordwave's top account-takeover vector. What should the team do?","options":["Strengthen the system prompt with capitalized warnings and three examples of urgent customers being politely refused, and move the rule to the very top of the prompt so it stays salient in long sessions.","Add a second Claude call after each conversation that reviews the transcript and alerts the fraud team whenever a SIM swap occurred without a prior verification step, so it can be reversed quickly.","Enforce the prerequisite in code: `initiate_sim_swap` is rejected unless session state holds a VERIFIED result from `verify_identity` for that account, returning an error that routes to verification.","Remove `initiate_sim_swap` from WaveAssist entirely and require every SIM swap to be escalated to a human agent, even after the customer passes identity verification and the account shows no fraud flags."],"answer":2,"explanation":"41/30,000이라는 낮은 비율이라도 SIM swap 사기는 계정 탈취로 직결되는 high-stakes 경로이므로, 확률적으로 따르는 프롬프트 지시로는 충분하지 않습니다. 필요한 것은 programmatic prerequisite gate입니다. 도구 계층(또는 tool-call 차단 로직)이 세션 상태에 해당 계정의 VERIFIED 결과가 있는지 확인하고, 없으면 실행을 거부하면서 \"먼저 verify_identity를 수행하라\"는 구조화된 오류를 돌려주면 됩니다. 이렇게 하면 고객이 긴급함을 호소해도 순서가 결정론적으로 보장되고, 오류 메시지가 에이전트를 올바른 다음 단계로 안내합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 반드시 지켜야 하는 단계 순서는 프롬프트가 아니라 코드로 강제(prerequisite gate) — Task Statement 1.4 · 출처: Section 5 (L28–L29)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 대문자 경고와 예시는 준수율을 높일 뿐 0으로 만들지 못합니다. 고위험 경로에서 전형적인 prompt-only fix 함정입니다.\n- B: 사후 탐지는 이미 SIM이 넘어간 뒤에 알림을 줄 뿐 예방하지 못합니다.\n- D: 과잉 대응입니다. 검증된 고객까지 모두 사람에게 넘기면 first-contact resolution 목표를 해치고, 정당한 자동 처리 경로를 불필요하게 없앱니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"MUST\"라는 프롬프트 규칙이 소수 사례에서 깨지고 결과가 심각하다면, 정답은 코드 수준 강제입니다.","id":"scenario-b-34","task":"1.4","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer opens with: \"I've been on hold twice already. I want to talk to a real person about my contract, not a bot.\" WaveAssist checks the account, sees a simple early-upgrade eligibility question it could answer in one tool call, and replies, \"I can help with that right away! You're eligible to upgrade on 12 November…\" The customer leaves a one-star review. How should the escalation logic handle this case?","options":["Have WaveAssist answer the question first and then offer a human, since resolving the issue in the same contact is the most effective way to improve first-contact resolution.","Treat an explicit request for a human as an immediate escalation trigger, calling `escalate_to_agent` with a handoff summary rather than attempting to resolve the question first.","Escalate only when a sentiment classifier scores the customer's message below a frustration threshold, so that mildly annoyed customers can still be helped by the agent.","Ask the customer to confirm the request twice and explain the expected queue wait time, escalating only if they still insist after hearing that the agent can solve it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"고객이 명시적으로 사람을 요청한 경우는 대표적인 escalation trigger입니다. 문제가 간단해서 에이전트가 해결할 수 있더라도, 고객의 명확한 의사를 무시하고 해결을 시도하는 것은 신뢰를 떨어뜨립니다. 올바른 동작은 즉시 `escalate_to_agent`를 호출하되, 고객 신원, 문의 내용, 이미 확인한 계정 정보(예: 업그레이드 가능일)를 담은 handoff summary를 함께 넘겨 사람이 다시 묻지 않게 하는 것입니다. 이것이 Nordwave의 \"다시 묻지 않는 escalation\" 목표와도 맞습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 명시적인 사람 요청은 즉시 escalation + 실행 가능한 handoff payload — Task Statement 5.2 · 출처: Section 17 (L114–L115)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: FCR 지표를 위해 고객 의사를 무시하는 설계입니다. 명시적 요청을 먼저 존중해야 합니다.\n- C: sentiment 점수는 escalation 필요성을 잘 대변하지 못합니다. 차분하게 사람을 요청하는 고객을 놓치고, 감정적이지만 해결 가능한 고객을 과잉 escalation합니다.\n- D: 반복 확인과 설득은 이미 두 번 대기한 고객에게 마찰만 더하며, 명시적 요청을 사실상 무시하는 것입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"customer explicitly asks for a human\" → 해결 시도가 아니라 즉시 escalation(요약 포함)입니다.","id":"scenario-b-35","task":"5.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":2,"stem":"When a customer asks for a €200 goodwill credit, `issue_bill_credit` rejects it because credits above €150 need supervisor approval. The MCP server currently returns `{\"isError\": true, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Operation failed\"}]}` for this and for every other failure. WaveAssist retries the call four times, then tells the customer \"our system is down, please try later.\" What is the best change?","options":["Have the MCP server retry internally up to three times with exponential backoff before returning any error, so the agent only sees failures that persist after retrying.","Return HTTP 403 from the MCP server for policy rejections and HTTP 503 for outages, and let the agent infer the cause of each failure from the status code it receives.","Add a system-prompt instruction that whenever a credit fails, the agent should assume a policy limit was hit and escalate to a supervisor rather than retrying the call.","Return structured error content with an error category (e.g. business_rule), an `isRetryable` flag set to false, the €150 limit, and the suggested next step of supervisor approval."],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"Operation failed\" 같은 generic error는 에이전트가 일시적 장애(transient)와 업무 규칙 위반(business rule)을 구분할 수 없게 만들어, 재시도해도 소용없는 요청을 반복하고 고객에게 잘못된 설명을 하게 됩니다. MCP 도구는 `isError: true`와 함께 errorCategory(transient / validation / business_rule / permission 등), isRetryable, 사람이 읽을 수 있는 원인(€150 한도), 권장 다음 단계(supervisor approval 또는 escalation)를 담은 structured error를 돌려줘야 합니다. 그러면 에이전트는 재시도를 멈추고 고객에게 정확히 설명한 뒤 승인 경로로 넘길 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 오류는 카테고리 + 재시도 가능 여부 + 원인 + 다음 행동을 담은 구조화된 tool result로 반환 — Task Statement 2.2 · 출처: Section 6 (L37–L38)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 업무 규칙 위반은 재시도해도 결과가 같습니다. 내부 재시도는 transient 오류에만 의미가 있고, 원인이 여전히 에이전트에게 전달되지 않습니다.\n- B: 정보가 HTTP 상태 코드에만 있으면 모델이 보는 tool result에는 반영되지 않습니다. 오류 정보는 모델이 읽는 tool result content에 있어야 합니다.\n- C: 모든 실패를 정책 한도로 가정하면 실제 장애나 입력 오류까지 잘못 escalation합니다. 근본 원인인 불명확한 오류 응답을 고치지 않는 prompt-only fix입니다.\n\n시험 팁: 에이전트가 의미 없는 재시도를 반복한다면 \"isRetryable + errorCategory가 담긴 structured error\"를 찾으세요.","id":"scenario-b-36","task":"2.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":1,"stem":"WaveAssist's tools wrap three backends. The billing mainframe returns amounts in integer cents and dates as `DDMMYYYY`; the CRM returns euro decimals and ISO 8601 timestamps; the network API returns Unix epoch seconds and numeric status codes like `3` for \"degraded.\" WaveAssist regularly misreads `11250` as €11,250 and compares outage times incorrectly against charge dates. The MCP servers belong to other teams and cannot change this quarter. What is the most effective approach?","options":["Register a PostToolUse hook in the Agent SDK that converts each tool result to one canonical format (euro decimals, ISO 8601 UTC, named statuses) before the model processes it.","Add a detailed conversion table to the system prompt explaining each backend's units and date formats, and instruct the model to convert all values before reasoning about them.","Register a PreToolUse hook that rewrites every tool call's input parameters into each backend's native format, so that the agent and the backends always agree on units.","Add a dedicated normalization subagent that receives every raw tool result from the coordinator, converts the values, and returns a cleaned version for the coordinator to use."],"answer":0,"explanation":"문제는 tool result가 모델에 도달할 때 형식이 제각각이라는 점이고, MCP 서버는 바꿀 수 없습니다. 이 경우 Agent SDK의 PostToolUse hook으로 도구 실행 직후, 모델이 결과를 처리하기 전에 결과를 가로채 금액·날짜·상태 코드를 하나의 canonical format으로 정규화하는 것이 가장 효과적입니다. 이 방식은 결정론적이며 모든 도구 호출에 일관되게 적용되고, 모델이 매번 단위 변환을 추론할 필요가 없습니다. 서버 소유 팀과 무관하게 에이전트 측에서 즉시 적용할 수 있다는 점도 제약 조건에 맞습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 이질적 데이터 형식 정규화 = 결과를 모델 처리 전에 가로채는 PostToolUse hook — Task Statement 1.5 · 출처: Section 12 (L80), Section 5 (L30)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 모델에게 변환을 맡기는 prompt-only 접근이라 바로 지금 관찰된 오독(11250 → €11,250)을 확률적으로만 줄입니다.\n- C: PreToolUse는 도구 호출 입력을 다룹니다. 문제는 출력 형식이므로 타이밍이 틀린 hook입니다(right idea, wrong event).\n- D: 결정론적 변환에 LLM 서브에이전트를 쓰는 것은 과잉 설계이며, 지연과 비용을 늘리고 변환 자체도 비결정적으로 만듭니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"도구 결과의 형식이 제각각이고 서버는 못 바꾼다\" → PostToolUse hook으로 정규화.","id":"scenario-b-37","task":"1.5","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer disputes €64 of roaming charges from a trip to Morocco. The billing subagent queries `get_usage_records`, but the mainframe times out on the roaming partition after 30 seconds. The subagent returns to the coordinator: `\"No roaming usage found for the requested period.\"` The coordinator tells the customer the charges must be a display error and issues a €64 credit. What is the best fix?","options":["Have the coordinator always repeat the subagent's query itself before acting on any result that is empty, so that every empty finding is independently confirmed by a second call.","Make the billing subagent retry the query until it succeeds, increasing the timeout on each attempt, so that it never returns to the coordinator until it has a definitive answer.","Instruct the coordinator in its system prompt to treat any empty result from a subagent with suspicion and to ask the customer for proof before it issues any credit.","Have the subagent return a structured status that separates \"query failed\" (timeout, partition, what was tried) from \"succeeded with zero results,\" plus any partial data."],"answer":3,"explanation":"이 사고의 원인은 access failure(타임아웃)가 valid empty result(\"기록 없음\")로 위장되어 전파된 것입니다. 이것이 대표적인 silent failure로, 코디네이터는 정상적인 \"없음\"으로 믿고 잘못된 크레딧을 발급했습니다. 서브에이전트는 propagation contract에 따라 실패 여부, 실패 유형, 시도한 내용(어떤 파티션, 어떤 기간), 확보한 partial results를 구조적으로 구분해 반환해야 합니다. 그래야 코디네이터가 재시도, 범위 축소, 또는 escalation 중 무엇을 할지 올바르게 판단할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: \"조회 실패\"와 \"조회 성공·결과 0건\"을 구분하는 구조화된 오류 전파 — Task Statement 5.3 · 출처: Section 17 (L117–L118)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 모든 빈 결과를 재조회하는 것은 비용이 크고, 서브에이전트가 정보를 숨기는 근본 원인을 고치지 않습니다.\n- B: 무한 재시도는 고객 대화를 멈추게 하고, 장애가 길면 결국 끝나지 않습니다. 실패는 숨기지 말고 상위로 알려 결정하게 해야 합니다.\n- C: 빈 결과를 모두 의심하라는 지시는 진짜 \"없음\"까지 의심하게 만들며, 실패 정보가 전달되지 않는 구조는 그대로입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"empty result인데 사실은 timeout\"이 보이면, 실패와 빈 결과를 구분하는 구조화된 상태 반환이 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-38","task":"5.3","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":2,"stem":"To simplify configuration, every WaveAssist agent was given the full set of 18 MCP tools. A review finds that the network-diagnostics subagent, while investigating a slow-data complaint, called `issue_bill_credit` for €20 \"as a goodwill gesture,\" and that it sometimes calls `get_bill_statement` instead of `check_outage_status`. What is the best change?","options":["Give each subagent only the tools its role needs, e.g. outage, cell-site, and provisioning tools for diagnostics, and keep credit-issuing tools out of the diagnostics subagent.","Keep all 18 tools on every agent but add a line to the diagnostics subagent's prompt stating that it must never issue credits and should focus only on network issues.","Keep all tools available but set `tool_choice` to `{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"check_outage_status\"}` on every diagnostics request so the subagent cannot choose any other tool.","Merge the diagnostics subagent into the coordinator so a single agent with all 18 tools handles everything and no subagent can act outside the coordinator's view."],"answer":0,"explanation":"모든 에이전트에 모든 도구를 주면 두 가지 문제가 생깁니다. 역할 밖의 행동(진단 서브에이전트의 크레딧 발급)이 가능해지고, 선택지가 많아져 tool-selection 정확도가 떨어집니다. Least privilege 원칙에 따라 각 서브에이전트에는 역할에 필요한 도구만 주어야 합니다. 진단 서브에이전트에서 `issue_bill_credit`을 아예 제거하면 잘못된 크레딧은 구조적으로 불가능해지고, 도구 수가 줄어 오선택도 감소합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 도구는 역할별로 최소한만 배분(less is more, least privilege) — Task Statement 2.3 · 출처: Section 6 (L39)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 권한이 있는 상태에서 \"하지 말라\"는 지시에 의존하는 prompt-only fix입니다. 도구 과다로 인한 오선택도 그대로 남습니다.\n- C: 매 요청마다 특정 도구를 강제하면 진단 과정에서 필요한 cell-site 조회나 provisioning 확인을 할 수 없어 서브에이전트가 제 기능을 못 합니다.\n- D: 단일 에이전트에 18개 도구를 몰아주면 선택 혼란이 더 커지고, 역할 격리라는 서브에이전트 설계의 이점도 사라집니다.\n\n시험 팁: 서브에이전트가 역할 밖 도구를 호출한다면, 정답은 프롬프트가 아니라 해당 도구를 빼는 것입니다.","id":"scenario-b-39","task":"2.3","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":1,"stem":"For complaints like \"my data stopped working and I was still charged for a day pass,\" the coordinator first delegates to the network-diagnostics subagent, waits for its findings (about 25 seconds), and then delegates to the billing-investigation subagent (another 30 seconds). Neither subagent needs the other's output; the coordinator combines both before replying. Customers abandon about 18% of these chats while waiting. What is the best change?","options":["Merge both subagents into a single combined subagent that holds the network and billing tools together, so that one delegation covers the entire complaint.","Have the coordinator issue both subagent delegations in the same response so they run in parallel, then aggregate both results before replying to the customer.","Let the network subagent call the billing subagent directly when it finishes, so the coordinator only waits for one final combined result to arrive at the end.","Reduce each subagent's max turns so it returns sooner, and accept less complete findings as a trade-off in exchange for a shorter wait for these customers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"두 작업은 서로의 출력에 의존하지 않는 독립 작업이므로 순차 실행할 이유가 없습니다. 코디네이터는 한 번의 응답에서 두 서브에이전트 호출(예: 두 개의 Task/Agent tool call)을 함께 내보내 parallel로 실행하고, 결과가 모두 돌아오면 aggregate해서 답변하면 됩니다. 그러면 대기 시간이 약 55초에서 약 30초(가장 느린 작업 시간)로 줄어듭니다. 코디네이터가 위임과 결과 통합을 모두 소유하는 hub-and-spoke 구조도 유지되어 관찰 가능성이 떨어지지 않습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 독립적인 하위 작업은 코디네이터가 한 턴에 병렬로 위임하고 결과를 통합 — Task Statement 1.2 · 출처: Section 4 (L16)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 역할 분리를 없애 도구 수가 늘고 컨텍스트가 섞이며, 두 조사를 한 에이전트가 순차로 처리하므로 시간도 크게 줄지 않습니다.\n- C: 서브에이전트 간 직접 호출은 코디네이터의 통제와 관찰을 우회하고, 여전히 순차 실행이라 지연도 해결되지 않습니다.\n- D: 지연의 원인은 순차 실행이지 조사 깊이가 아닙니다. 품질을 희생하는 잘못된 trade-off입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"서로의 출력이 필요 없는데 순차로 실행\" → 한 응답에서 병렬 위임.","id":"scenario-b-40","task":"1.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":5,"stem":"WaveAssist asks Claude to rate its confidence (0–1) that a disputed charge is a billing error. Credits under €150 are auto-approved when confidence is at least 0.90; everything else goes to a human review queue. A quarterly audit shows that 18% of auto-approved credits at stated confidence 0.90–0.95 were not actually billing errors, while overall accuracy looks fine because most disputes are simple. What should the team do?","options":["Raise the auto-approval threshold from 0.90 to 0.98 and tell the model in its prompt to be more conservative whenever it estimates confidence for disputed charges.","Remove auto-approval entirely and send every dispute to human review until a newer model version is released that produces confidence scores the team can trust.","Calibrate the scores against a labeled validation set to set thresholds from measured accuracy, and keep stratified sampling of auto-approved credits by dispute type for audit.","Ask the model to explain its reasoning before giving the score and auto-approve only when the written explanation mentions at least two independent pieces of evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"모델이 스스로 말하는 self-reported confidence는 실제 정확도와 일치한다는 보장이 없습니다(0.90이라고 말했지만 실제 오류율 18%). 따라서 정답이 알려진 labeled validation set으로 점수 구간별 실제 정확도를 측정해 calibration하고, 그 측정값에 근거해 자동 승인 임계값을 정해야 합니다. 또한 전체 정확도는 쉬운 다수 사례에 가려 위험한 하위 유형의 오류를 숨기므로, 분쟁 유형별 stratified sampling으로 자동 승인 건을 지속적으로 감사해야 합니다. 이 조합이 자동화를 유지하면서 인간 검토를 가장 필요한 곳에 집중시킵니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 자기보고 confidence는 validation set으로 보정하고, 자동 처리 건은 계층화 표본으로 지속 감사 — Task Statement 5.5 · 출처: Section 19 (L127–L129)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 보정되지 않은 점수의 임계값만 올리는 것은 근거 없는 조정입니다. 0.98이라는 숫자도 실제 정확도와 연결되어 있지 않습니다.\n- B: 과잉 대응입니다. 자동화의 이점을 모두 포기하며, 새 모델이 나와도 보정 없이는 같은 문제가 생깁니다.\n- D: 설명 속 증거 개수는 정확도의 검증된 대리 지표가 아니며, 모델은 그럴듯한 근거를 쉽게 생성할 수 있습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"stated confidence ≠ actual accuracy\"가 보이면 validation set 기반 calibration + stratified sampling이 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-41","task":"5.5","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":2,"stem":"Nordwave's five WaveAssist engineers use Claude Code daily and want everyone to get the same `nordwave-billing-sandbox` MCP server automatically when they clone the repository. The server needs a per-developer sandbox token. One engineer proposes committing a config file containing the server definition with his own token pasted in. What is the best way to set this up?","options":["Have each engineer add the server with user scope so that it is stored in their personal Claude Code configuration and is available across all of their projects without touching the repository.","Define the server in a project-scoped `.mcp.json` committed to the repository, and have it read each developer's own token through environment-variable expansion such as `${BILLING_SANDBOX_TOKEN}`.","Commit the `.mcp.json` with the engineer's token as proposed, but restrict the repository's read access to the five WaveAssist engineers so the secret stays within the team and rotate the token every quarter.","Document the server's launch command and token setup in the project CLAUDE.md so that Claude Code reads the instructions and connects to the server automatically when each new session begins."],"answer":1,"explanation":"저장소를 클론한 팀원 모두가 같은 MCP 서버를 쓰게 하려면 project scope 설정인 `.mcp.json`을 저장소에 커밋하는 것이 맞습니다. 동시에 비밀값은 커밋하면 안 되므로, `.mcp.json`의 environment-variable expansion(`${BILLING_SANDBOX_TOKEN}`)으로 각 개발자가 자기 환경 변수에 토큰을 두게 합니다. 이렇게 하면 서버 정의는 공유되고 자격 증명은 개인별로 분리됩니다. 개발자별 토큰이라는 요구 사항도 자연스럽게 충족됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 팀 공유 MCP 서버 = 커밋된 project `.mcp.json` + `${VAR}` 환경 변수 확장으로 비밀 분리 — Task Statement 2.4 · 출처: Section 7 (L49), Section 8 (L55)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: user scope는 개인 설정이라 저장소와 함께 공유되지 않습니다. 개인용 서버에는 맞지만 팀 자동 공유 요구에는 맞지 않습니다.\n- C: 접근 제한이 있어도 비밀값이 Git 이력에 영구히 남고, 모든 팀원이 한 사람의 토큰을 쓰게 되어 개발자별 토큰 요구도 어깁니다.\n- D: CLAUDE.md는 지침과 컨텍스트를 제공할 뿐 MCP 서버를 등록·연결하지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"팀 공유 + 비밀값\"이면 project `.mcp.json` + `${ENV_VAR}` 조합을 고르세요.","id":"scenario-b-42","task":"2.4","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":1,"stem":"On Monday, WaveAssist escalated a customer's disputed early-termination fee and saved the session ID. On Tuesday morning, a human agent waived half the fee, moved the customer to a new plan, and handed the case back. The customer returns to chat on Tuesday afternoon. Monday's session contains 60 turns, including tool results that show the old plan and the full unwaived fee. How should WaveAssist continue the case?","options":["Resume Monday's session by its ID so that the agent keeps the full conversational context, and let the customer explain whatever has changed since then.","Start a new session seeded with a structured summary of Monday's case and the human's actions, and have the agent re-fetch the current account and bill state.","Fork Monday's session so that the original transcript is preserved for audit, and continue the conversation in the fork with all of Monday's tool results kept.","Start a new session and paste in Monday's complete 60-turn transcript as the first user message so that nothing from the earlier conversation is lost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Monday 세션의 핵심 tool result(기존 요금제, 감면 전 해지 수수료)는 사람이 개입한 뒤로 stale 상태가 되었습니다. 이를 그대로 resume하면 에이전트가 오래된 결과를 사실로 믿고 잘못된 금액을 안내할 위험이 큽니다. 이전 컨텍스트의 상당 부분이 무효화된 경우에는 새 세션을 시작하고, 사건 경위와 사람의 조치를 담은 structured summary를 주입한 뒤 현재 계정·청구 상태를 도구로 다시 조회하는 것이 안전합니다. 세션 재개는 대화 상태를 이어 줄 뿐 외부 시스템의 변화를 자동으로 반영하지 않는다는 점이 핵심입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 이전 tool result가 stale이면 resume보다 구조화된 요약 + 최신 상태 재조회로 새 세션 — Task Statement 1.7 · 출처: Section 4 (L22), Section 12 (L81)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 컨텍스트가 대부분 유효할 때는 resume이 맞지만, 여기서는 핵심 결과가 바뀌었습니다. 변경 사항을 고객에게 다시 설명하게 하는 것도 \"다시 묻지 않기\" 목표에 어긋납니다.\n- C: fork는 같은 기점에서 다른 접근을 탐색할 때 쓰는 분기 기능입니다. stale 결과를 그대로 물려받으므로 문제를 해결하지 못합니다.\n- D: 60턴 전체를 붙이면 stale 결과가 그대로 들어가고 컨텍스트만 낭비됩니다. 요약 없이 원문을 다시 넣는 것은 resume의 단점을 그대로 재현합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"중간에 외부 상태가 바뀜\" → resume이 아니라 요약 주입 + 재조회로 새 세션.","id":"scenario-b-43","task":"1.7","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer asks how much roaming she can be charged in Switzerland per month. WaveAssist retrieves three sources: her signed contract (2024, \"roaming charges capped at €50/month\"), the current public promotions page (2026, \"new Travel+ plans: €75/month cap\"), and an internal knowledge-base article that says \"caps vary by plan.\" WaveAssist answers, \"Your roaming is capped at €75 per month.\" What is the best change to how WaveAssist synthesizes answers?","options":["Always prefer the most recently dated source when sources disagree, since newer documents are more likely to reflect current pricing and the company's latest policy.","Keep source attribution and dates on each claim, surface the conflict instead of choosing silently, and apply the contract-governs rule or escalate when precedence is unclear.","Restrict WaveAssist to answering only from the internal knowledge base, because it is curated by Nordwave staff and is therefore the most authoritative source available.","Ask the model to give an averaged or middle-ground figure with a note that pricing may vary, so that the customer receives a reasonable estimate rather than conflicting numbers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"여러 출처가 충돌할 때 하나를 조용히 골라 단정하는 것이 이 오류의 원인입니다. 올바른 multi-source synthesis는 각 주장에 source attribution과 날짜(유효 시점)를 유지하고, 충돌을 conflict annotation으로 드러낸 뒤, 정해진 우선순위 규칙(여기서는 고객이 서명한 계약이 일반 프로모션보다 우선)을 적용하는 것입니다. 우선순위가 불명확하면 추측하지 말고 사람에게 escalation해야 합니다. 이렇게 하면 근거 추적이 가능해지고, 고객에게 계약과 다른 금액을 약속하는 위험을 막을 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 출처·날짜를 보존하고 충돌을 드러내며, 명시적 우선순위 규칙 또는 escalation으로 해결 — Task Statement 5.6 · 출처: Section 19 (L131–L132)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: \"최신이 우선\"은 그럴듯하지만, 프로모션 페이지는 신규 Travel+ 요금제에 해당하며 기존 계약 조건을 대체하지 않습니다. 날짜만으로 우선순위를 정하면 안 됩니다.\n- C: 지식베이스는 \"요금제마다 다름\"이라고만 할 뿐 이 고객의 답을 주지 못합니다. 가장 구체적이고 구속력 있는 계약을 버리는 것입니다.\n- D: 평균값은 어떤 출처에도 근거하지 않는 수치를 만들어 내며, 충돌을 해결하지 않고 숨기는 방식입니다.\n\n시험 팁: 출처 충돌 문제에서는 \"조용히 하나 고르기\"가 아니라 \"출처 표기 + 충돌 표면화 + 우선순위 규칙/escalation\"이 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-b-44","task":"5.6","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A caller says, \"This is Sofia Marchetti, I want to cancel my broadband.\" `get_account(name=\"Sofia Marchetti\")` returns two active accounts: a home-broadband account in Turin opened in 2019, and a family mobile plan in Milan opened last month on which Sofia Marchetti is listed as a secondary user. The current logic picks the most recently opened account. What should WaveAssist do?","options":["Select the Turin broadband account automatically because the customer said \"broadband,\" and proceed with the cancellation flow after reading the account address back.","Escalate to a human agent immediately, because any lookup returning more than one account indicates possible fraud and should never be handled by the automated agent.","Keep the most-recent-account rule but add a confirmation step before cancelling, reading the account number back to the customer to confirm it is the correct one.","Ask the customer for an additional identifier, such as the service address or account number, and match it before taking any action on either account."],"answer":3,"explanation":"이름 조회 결과가 여러 건일 때 heuristic(최근 개설 계정, 키워드)으로 하나를 고르면 잘못된 계정을 해지하는 되돌리기 어려운 오류가 생길 수 있습니다. 올바른 ambiguity resolution은 고객에게 서비스 주소나 계정 번호 같은 추가 식별자를 요청해 정확히 하나로 좁힌 뒤에만 행동하는 것입니다. 특히 해지처럼 irreversible한 작업에서는 추측 대신 확인이 원칙입니다. 이 과정은 한 번의 질문으로 끝나므로 first-contact resolution도 해치지 않습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 다중 일치 시 휴리스틱 선택 금지, 추가 식별자로 명확화한 뒤 행동 — Task Statement 5.2 · 출처: Section 17 (L119)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: \"broadband\"라는 단어도 휴리스틱입니다. 고객이 다른 주소의 회선을 말하는 것일 수도 있고, 동명이인의 계정일 가능성도 배제하지 못합니다.\n- B: 동명이인이나 가족 요금제처럼 다중 일치는 흔합니다. 이를 모두 사기로 보고 escalation하는 것은 과잉 대응이며 FCR을 해칩니다.\n- C: 잘못된 계정을 먼저 고른 뒤 번호만 읽어 주면 고객이 오류를 알아차리지 못할 수 있습니다. 확인 단계를 더해도 잘못된 선택 규칙은 그대로입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"여러 건이 조회됨\" → 휴리스틱으로 고르지 말고 고객에게 추가 식별 정보를 물으세요.","id":"scenario-b-45","task":"5.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Nordwave Telecom, a regional mobile and home-broadband carrier with about 2.4 million subscribers, is replacing its tier-1 chat queue with WaveAssist, a resolution agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and delegates focused work to two subagents: a billing-investigation subagent (bill line items, roaming and usage records, credits) and a network-diagnostics subagent (outage maps, cell-site status, device provisioning). All back-office access goes through MCP servers that expose tools such as `get_account`, `get_bill_statement`, `get_usage_records`, `check_outage_status`, `verify_identity`, `issue_bill_credit`, `change_plan`, `initiate_sim_swap`, and `escalate_to_agent`. These tools wrap three legacy systems (a 1990s billing mainframe, a modern CRM, and a network-operations API) that format dates, amounts, and status codes differently. Company policy is strict: any SIM swap requires a successful identity verification in the same session, credits above €150 require supervisor approval, and regulators audit every account change. Conversations are often long, because customers paste multi-month bills and switch between several issues in one chat. Escalated cases are picked up by human agents, sometimes the next business day, and may be returned to WaveAssist afterward. Nordwave's targets are 75% first-contact resolution, zero unauthorized account changes, and escalations that a human can act on without re-asking the customer anything."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The `record_bill_of_lading` schema marks `notify_party` (an object with `name` and `address`) as required. Negotiable \"TO ORDER\" bills often carry no notify party at all. Audits show that on those bills the extracted `notify_party` usually repeats the shipper or the consignee bank, or contains a plausible but invented company, and the TMS then sends arrival notices to the wrong firm. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Keep the field required and add a system-prompt rule that the model must never invent party names and should copy text verbatim from the document instead.","Keep the field required and fill it with a sentinel object such as `{\"name\": \"UNKNOWN\"}` whenever the model reports that no notify party block was found.","Add a validator that rejects outputs where `notify_party` matches the shipper or consignee, and re-prompt the model until a different party name is returned.","Make `notify_party` nullable, describe when null is correct (no notify block, or \"SAME AS CONSIGNEE\"), and update the TMS to skip notices on null."],"answer":3,"explanation":"원문에 항상 존재하지 않는 값을 required로 지정하면 모델은 무언가를 채우도록 압박을 받아 그럴듯한 hallucinated value를 만들어 냅니다. 근본 원인은 프롬프트가 아니라 스키마 설계이므로, `notify_party`를 nullable/optional로 바꾸고 description에 \"언제 null이 정답인지\"라는 boundary case를 적어야 합니다. 이렇게 하면 부재가 \"정상적인 예상 결과\"라는 신호가 모델과 하류 시스템 양쪽에 전달됩니다. 동시에 TMS가 null을 오류 없이 처리하도록 바꾸어야 부재와 존재의 구분이 끝까지 보존됩니다. strict 모드는 필수 필드 누락을 막아 줄 뿐이므로, 오히려 required 지정이 환각을 강제하는 방향으로 작용합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 기반 데이터가 매번 값을 보장할 때만 required — Task Statement 4.3 · 출처: Section 15 (L98)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 프롬프트 지시만으로는 스키마가 만드는 \"반드시 채워라\" 압박을 이기지 못합니다. 지시와 스키마가 충돌하는 상태가 그대로 남습니다.\n- B: sentinel 기본값은 \"추출된 값\"과 \"찾지 못함\"의 구분을 흐리게 하고, 하류 TMS가 \"UNKNOWN\"이라는 회사에 통지를 보낼 위험이 있습니다.\n- C: 다른 이름을 강요하는 재시도는 새로운 날조를 유도할 뿐입니다. 값이 정말 없는 문서에 재시도는 답이 될 수 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"값이 없는 문서에서 환각\" → 프롬프트·재시도보다 required/nullable 스키마 설계가 먼저입니다.","id":"scenario-b-46","task":"4.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Shipment packets are 10–40 page PDFs that combine a bill of lading, a packing list, a DGD, and sometimes a delivery receipt. The current design sends the whole packet in one request with one large schema containing every field of every document type. Results show field bleed: packing-list carton counts land in the bill of lading's `package_count`, and DGD emergency phone numbers appear as the notify party's phone. What is the best redesign?","options":["Segment the packet first by classifying page ranges by document type, run each segment through its own type-specific schema, then reconcile shared keys in a separate step.","Keep the single request but switch to a larger model with extended thinking enabled, so it can reason about which page each value came from before filling in any field of the schema.","Split the packet into single pages and extract every page independently with the combined schema, then merge non-null values page by page into one shipment record.","Keep the combined schema but prefix every field name with its document type, such as `bol_package_count`, so the model can tell which document each field belongs to."],"answer":0,"explanation":"여러 문서 유형이 섞인 입력을 하나의 거대 스키마로 한 번에 처리하는 monolithic 설계가 필드 혼동의 근본 원인입니다. 먼저 페이지 범위를 문서 유형별로 segmentation/classification하고, 각 구간을 해당 유형 전용 스키마로 추출하면 각 하위 작업이 single responsibility와 명확한 입력을 갖게 됩니다. 그 뒤 booking 번호나 컨테이너 번호 같은 공통 키는 별도의 reconciliation 단계에서 교차 확인합니다. 이 구조는 실패한 구간만 재시도할 수 있게 해 주고(targeted error recovery), 독립 구간은 병렬 처리도 가능합니다. capability/document boundary가 자연스러운 분해 지점이라는 원칙을 그대로 적용한 설계입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 서로 다른 문서 경계에서 분해하고, 공통 키는 별도 단계에서 결합 — Task Statement 1.6 · 출처: Section 3 (L10, L11)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 더 강한 모델과 추론은 증상을 줄일 수는 있어도, 한 스키마가 여러 문서를 섞어 받는 구조적 원인은 그대로입니다.\n- C: 페이지 단위는 over-decomposition입니다. 여러 페이지에 걸친 BoL 정보가 끊기고, 병합 규칙이 새 오류를 만듭니다.\n- D: 이름 접두어는 약간의 단서를 줄 뿐, 한 요청에 모든 문서와 모든 필드가 섞여 있는 상황은 바뀌지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 여러 유형이 섞인 입력의 필드 혼동 → 분류·분할 후 유형별 추출, 마지막에 reconciliation.","id":"scenario-b-47","task":"1.6","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":2,"stem":"During a 40-minute outage of the hazmat reference database, the MCP tool `lookup_un_number` caught the timeout and returned a normal result: `{\"matches\": []}`. The extraction agent read this as \"this UN number does not exist\" and marked 312 dangerous-goods shipments as `un_number_invalid`, which put them all on customs hold. The same empty response is returned when a UN number truly is not in the list. What change best prevents this?","options":["Have the agent call `lookup_un_number` three times whenever the result is empty, and only mark the UN number invalid if all three calls return no matches.","Return timeouts with `is_error: true` and content giving an error category, retryable flag, and the queried value; keep a true miss as a successful `not_found` result.","Add a system-prompt note saying that empty lookup results can sometimes be caused by outages, so the agent should be careful before marking any UN number as invalid on a shipment.","Return the raw database exception and stack trace in the tool result content so the agent can read the underlying error and decide what it means for the shipment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"근본 원인은 access failure(timeout)와 valid empty result(진짜 not found)가 똑같은 성공 응답으로 반환된 것, 즉 오류를 삼킨 silent failure입니다. 도구는 실패 시 `tool_result`에 `is_error: true`를 설정하고, content 안에 error category(transient/timeout), retryable 여부, 실패한 입력값 같은 구조화된 정보를 담아야 합니다. 반면 UN 번호가 목록에 실제로 없는 경우는 실패가 아니라 정상적인 조회 결과이므로 성공 응답으로 `not_found`를 명시합니다. 이렇게 구분하면 에이전트는 timeout에는 재시도나 보류를, 진짜 미존재에는 무효 판정을 각각 올바르게 선택할 수 있습니다. 코드를 안정적인 문자열로 유지하면 라우팅 규칙도 버전과 무관하게 동작합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 접근 실패와 정상적인 빈 결과를 구분하는 structured error (`is_error` + category + retryable) — Task Statement 2.2 · 출처: Section 6 (L37)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 장애가 40분 지속되면 세 번 모두 빈 결과가 나와 같은 오판이 반복됩니다. 신호 자체가 구분되지 않는 문제를 고치지 못합니다.\n- C: 응답이 같으면 에이전트가 원인을 구별할 정보가 없습니다. 프롬프트로 \"조심하라\"는 것은 판단 근거를 주지 못합니다.\n- D: 원시 stack trace는 노이즈이며, 오류를 성공 응답 안에 묻어 두는 것은 대표적 실수입니다. 기계가 읽는 분류와 retryable 정보가 필요합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"빈 결과\"가 장애인지 진짜 없음인지 구분 못 하는 도구 → `is_error` + 오류 범주 + retryable.","id":"scenario-b-48","task":"2.2","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The team wants to cut costs by moving work to the Message Batches API. Three workloads are proposed: (1) the one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents, due within six weeks; (2) customs pre-filing extraction, which must finish before a cutoff a few hours after each booking arrives; (3) the exception-resolution agent, which calls `freight-reference` lookups and decides its next step from each result. Which plan is best?","options":["Batch only workload 1, tagging each request with the document ID as `custom_id` and joining results by it; keep workloads 2 and 3 on the synchronous API.","Batch workloads 1 and 3, since batch requests support tool definitions; keep workload 2 synchronous because its filing cutoff is too close for the 24-hour window.","Batch all three workloads, submitting workload 2 as soon as each booking arrives, since most batches finish within an hour and the discount is 50 percent.","Batch workloads 1 and 2 with results matched by submission order, and keep only workload 3 synchronous, because it is the only one that needs tool calls."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Message Batches API는 50% 할인 대신 최대 24시간 처리 창을 가지며, 그 안에서 지연 보장은 없습니다. 6주 기한의 아카이브 backfill은 아무도 기다리지 않는 작업이라 배치에 이상적이며, 결과는 완료 순서로 오므로 `custom_id`로 원본 문서와 매칭해야 합니다. 몇 시간 안에 끝나야 하는 customs pre-filing은 \"보통 1시간\"이라는 약속되지 않은 기대에 의존할 수 없으므로 동기 처리입니다. exception-resolution 에이전트는 도구 결과를 받아 다음 행동을 결정하는 multi-turn agentic loop인데, 배치 요청은 한 번 제출하고 한 번 반환되는 single turn이라 요청 중간에 도구를 실행하고 결과를 되먹일 수 없습니다. 따라서 배치는 1번만 해당합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: \"이 작업을 기다리는 것이 있는가?\" + 배치는 single-turn, `custom_id`로 상관 — Task Statement 4.5 · 출처: Section 15 (L106)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 배치가 도구 정의를 지원하는 것은 맞지만, 요청 중간의 도구 실행·결과 반환 왕복은 불가능해 agentic loop에는 맞지 않습니다.\n- C: 24시간은 추정치가 아니라 상한입니다. 마감이 있는 filing에 배치를 쓰면 할인이 아니라 예약된 장애가 됩니다.\n- D: 제출 순서로 결과를 매칭하면 오류 없이 엉뚱한 레코드에 데이터가 붙습니다. 2번의 마감 문제도 남습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 배치 = 지연 허용 + single-turn + `custom_id` 매칭. 마감·대화형·agentic loop는 동기.","id":"scenario-b-49","task":"4.5","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"About 2% of extractions fail the ISO 6346 check-digit rule on `container_number`, usually because a smudged \"8\" was read as \"B\" or \"0\" as \"O\". The current retry sends: \"Your output failed validation. Please try again.\" Logs show the second and third attempts almost always fail the same check on the same container, and failed records are then silently dropped from the TMS feed. What is the best redesign?","options":["Re-prompt with the failing field, expected vs computed check digit, and the source region, asking to re-read only that field; cap at two retries, then send it to human review.","Keep the generic retry message but raise the limit to ten attempts and increase temperature on each attempt so the model eventually produces a container number that passes.","Write a post-processor that swaps visually similar characters such as B/8 and O/0 until the check digit passes, and accept the first variant that validates without re-prompting.","Ask for the full record again in the retry, including all fields, so the model can rebuild the extraction from scratch and fix any inconsistencies it notices along the way."],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"다시 시도하라\"는 일반적인 재프롬프트는 무엇이 틀렸는지 알려 주지 않아 같은 실패를 거의 그대로 재현합니다. 효과적인 retry는 구체적 검증 오류(어느 필드, 기대 check digit과 계산값), 관련 원문 영역을 다시 포함해 기억이 아니라 증거에서 재추출하게 하고, 실패 필드만 고치도록 범위를 좁혀야 합니다. 또 retry budget은 2~3회로 작게 두고, 소진되면 빈 결과를 조용히 버리지 말고 사람 검토 큐로 명시적으로 escalation해야 합니다. 현재 설계의 \"silently dropped\"는 가장 위험한 실패 모드인 silence에 해당합니다. A는 피드백 품질, 범위, 예산, escalation을 모두 해결합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 구체적 오류 + 원문 + 실패 필드만 수정 + 작은 retry budget + 명시적 escalation — Task Statement 4.4 · 출처: Section 15 (L101, L102)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 피드백이 그대로이면 시도 횟수를 늘려도 같은 실패가 반복되고, 높은 temperature는 우연히 검사를 통과하는 잘못된 번호를 만들 수 있습니다.\n- C: check digit을 맞추는 문자 치환은 원문 근거 없이 \"통과하는 값\"을 고르는 것이라, 실제와 다른 컨테이너 번호가 검증을 통과할 수 있습니다.\n- D: 전체 재생성은 이미 맞은 필드에 새 오류를 만들 수 있으며, 무엇이 틀렸는지에 대한 정보도 여전히 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: Retry 프롬프트에는 \"무엇이 왜 틀렸나 + 원문 + 그 필드만\", 예산 소진 시 사람에게.","id":"scenario-b-50","task":"4.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":1,"stem":"The exception-resolution agent runs a manual loop with the Messages API. A reviewer finds this exit check:\n\nresponse = client.messages.create(model=MODEL, tools=TOOLS, messages=msgs)\nif response.content[0].type == \"text\":\n    break  # agent is finished\n\nOn many shipments the agent stops after writing \"Let me check the carrier SCAC first,\" and the lookup it requested in that same response is never executed. What is the best fix?","options":["Set `tool_choice` to `{\"type\": \"any\"}` on every turn so the model always starts its response with a tool call instead of a short narrative text block.","Check the final text for a phrase such as \"RESOLUTION COMPLETE\" and keep looping until the model writes it, with a system-prompt rule telling it to end that way.","Raise `max_tokens` so the model has room to put the narrative and tool call in separate turns, and keep the existing first-block check as the exit condition.","Loop on `stop_reason`: run the tools and return results while it is `tool_use`, end on `end_turn`, and enforce a hard iteration cap in the orchestration code."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Claude는 한 응답 안에 설명 텍스트 블록과 그 뒤의 `tool_use` 블록을 함께 낼 수 있으므로, 첫 블록이 텍스트인지로 종료를 판단하면 도구 호출이 남아 있는데도 루프가 끝납니다. 올바른 루프 제어는 `stop_reason`을 기준으로, `tool_use`이면 모든 도구를 실행해 `tool_result`를 돌려주고 계속하며, `end_turn`이면 종료하는 것입니다. 여기에 runtime layer의 hard iteration cap을 함께 두어 폭주 루프를 막아야 합니다. 이 구조는 모델의 자연어 자기 보고에 의존하지 않으므로 결정적이고 감사 가능합니다. 문제는 모델 행동이 아니라 루프 코드의 종료 조건에 있었습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: agentic loop의 계속/종료는 `stop_reason`으로, 반복 상한은 코드로 — Task Statement 1.1 · 출처: Section 2 (L4, L6)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: `any`로 강제하면 모델이 텍스트로 끝낼 방법이 사라져 루프가 끝나지 않을 위험이 생깁니다. 서두 텍스트를 없애는 것이 문제의 본질도 아닙니다.\n- B: 자연어 문구 파싱은 불안정하고 모델의 자기 보고를 종료 신호로 삼는 안티패턴입니다.\n- C: 토큰 한도는 이 버그와 무관합니다. 잘못된 첫 블록 검사가 그대로 남아 같은 조기 종료가 계속됩니다.\n\n시험 팁: 루프 종료 = `stop_reason` (`tool_use` 계속 / `end_turn` 종료) + 코드 수준 상한.","id":"scenario-b-51","task":"1.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The bill-of-lading prompt includes four few-shot examples, all taken from one carrier's layout and all showing gross weight in kilograms (\"KGS\"). In production, bills that state weight in \"LBS\" or \"MT\", or show both units, often come back with `gross_weight_kg` holding the pound figure unconverted or the metric tons value treated as kilograms. Bills with no weight at all sometimes show a weight copied from the measurement column. What should the team do?","options":["Add six more examples from the same carrier so the model sees a larger and more consistent pattern, and move the cleanest example to the very end of the block.","Keep the four examples and add an instruction in capitals saying the model must always check the weight unit carefully before filling in the weight field.","Replace the set with a few varied examples (LBS, MT, dual-unit, no weight given) whose outputs show the source unit, a correct conversion, and null when absent.","Switch to dynamic few-shot selection that retrieves the most similar examples at runtime, using the four existing kilogram examples as the retrieval pool."],"answer":2,"explanation":"모든 예시가 한 carrier 형식과 KGS 단위에서 나왔기 때문에 모델은 \"무게는 늘 kg\"이라는 좁은 패턴 하나만 학습했습니다. 이것은 diversity 부족과 example contamination 문제이며, 처방은 LBS, MT, 이중 단위, 무게 없음 같은 edge case를 포함한 다양한 예시로 교체하는 것입니다. 각 예시의 output은 원 단위 기록, 정확한 변환, 값이 없을 때의 null까지 정답 그 자체를 보여 주어야 합니다. 잘 고른 다양한 예시 3~4개가 같은 영역의 많은 예시보다 낫습니다. 나쁜 예시는 추가 지시로 땜질하지 말고 교체해야 합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 예시는 양이 아니라 커버리지의 폭, 경계 사례 포함 — Task Statement 4.2 · 출처: Section 14 (L90)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 같은 carrier 예시를 더 넣으면 좁은 패턴이 오히려 강화됩니다. 순서 조정은 다양성 부족을 해결하지 못합니다.\n- B: 나쁜 예시를 유지한 채 지시로 보완하는 것은 시험 함정입니다. 예시가 보여 주는 패턴이 지시보다 강하게 작용합니다.\n- D: dynamic few-shot은 좋은 기법이지만, pool이 kg 예시 네 개뿐이면 어떤 입력에도 같은 좁은 예시가 선택됩니다.\n\n시험 팁: Few-shot 실패 → 지시 추가가 아니라 다양하고 경계를 시험하는 예시로 교체.","id":"scenario-b-52","task":"4.2","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The `freight-reference` MCP server exposes these two tools to the extraction agent:\n\n{\"name\": \"lookup_party\", \"description\": \"Looks up a party.\"}\n{\"name\": \"lookup_carrier\", \"description\": \"Looks up carrier info.\"}\n\nLogs show the agent often calls `lookup_party` with four-letter SCAC codes like \"MAEU\" and calls `lookup_carrier` with shipper names like \"Kestrel Foods GmbH,\" so both calls return no match. What is the most effective first fix?","options":["Add three worked examples of correct tool calls to the system prompt so the agent learns which kinds of identifiers go to which of the two lookup tools.","Rename the tools to `find_shipping_party_record` and `find_ocean_carrier_record` while keeping the current descriptions, so the names make each tool's purpose clearer.","Rewrite each description: what input it takes (SCAC code vs party name or EORI), what it returns, an example input, and when to use the other tool instead.","Detect four-letter uppercase tokens in application code and set `tool_choice` to force `lookup_carrier` whenever the next request contains such a token."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Claude는 도구를 고를 때 주로 tool description을 근거로 삼으므로, \"Looks up a party\"처럼 이름만 반복하는 설명은 라우팅 정보를 전혀 주지 않습니다. 효과적인 설명은 어떤 입력을 받는지(4자리 SCAC 코드 vs 당사자 이름/EORI), 무엇을 반환하는지, 예시 입력, 그리고 언제 다른 도구를 써야 하는지라는 경계를 명시합니다. 이렇게 하면 비슷해 보이는 두 도구의 boundary가 분명해져 오선택이 근본적으로 줄어듭니다. 설명 개선은 비용이 가장 낮고 영향이 가장 큰 첫 조치입니다. 다른 방법은 설명이 부실한 상태를 그대로 두고 주변을 보완할 뿐입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 도구 선택 오류의 1차 수단은 입력·반환·경계를 담은 description — Task Statement 2.1 · 출처: Section 6 (L32, L33)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: few-shot 예시는 보조 수단일 뿐이며, 도구 정의 자체의 모호함이 남아 새로운 식별자 형식에서 다시 혼동됩니다.\n- B: 이름이 조금 나아져도 입력 형식과 사용 경계를 설명하지 않으면 모델은 여전히 추측해야 합니다.\n- D: 정규식 기반 강제 라우팅은 깨지기 쉽고(예: 4자리 대문자 약어), 모델의 판단을 우회하는 과잉 설계입니다.\n\n시험 팁: 비슷한 도구 간 오선택 → 먼저 description에 입력 형식·반환·사용/비사용 경계를 씁니다.","id":"scenario-b-53","task":"2.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The bill-of-lading subagent sets `is_dangerous_goods: true` on about 18% of bills, but only 4% actually carry hazmat. Review shows the flag is triggered by the printed terms on the back page (\"Shipper warrants that no flammable or explosive goods...\"), by phrases like \"NOT RESTRICTED,\" and by product names such as \"Fire Extinguisher Cabinets (empty).\" Each false flag costs a manual DG review. What change will most reduce these false positives?","options":["Instruct the model to be more conservative and to set the flag only when it is highly confident, since unnecessary flags cost the review desk time.","Ask the model to output a confidence score with the flag, and only send bills with a score above 0.85 to the dangerous-goods review desk.","Define the flag: true only if the cargo lines give a UN number, shipping name, and hazard class; boilerplate and \"NOT RESTRICTED\" do not count.","Add a second model call that reviews every bill flagged as dangerous goods and asks whether the flag looks correct before sending it to the review desk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"거짓 양성의 근본 원인은 \"dangerous goods\"가 무엇인지에 대한 판단 기준이 정의되지 않은 것입니다. 정밀도를 높이는 가장 효과적인 방법은 explicit criteria, 즉 이 화물의 cargo 설명에 UN 번호, proper shipping name, hazard class가 있을 때만 true라는 포함 조건과, 뒷면 약관 문구, \"NOT RESTRICTED\", 위험물이 아닌 제품명 같은 명시적 제외 조건을 함께 주는 것입니다. 이렇게 하면 모델이 문맥만으로 추측하던 경계가 규칙으로 바뀌어 일관성이 생깁니다. \"더 신중하라\" 같은 모호한 지시나 자기 보고 confidence는 기준 자체를 바꾸지 않습니다. 기준을 먼저 고친 뒤에도 남는 오류는 검증이나 리뷰 단계에서 다룹니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 거짓 양성 감소 = 모호한 \"신중하라\"가 아니라 포함/제외 조건이 명시된 기준 — Task Statement 4.1 · 출처: Section 13 (L83, L84)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: \"conservative\", \"confident\"는 무엇이 해당하는지 알려 주지 않는 모호한 지시라 효과가 불안정합니다.\n- B: 모델의 자기 보고 confidence는 잘 보정되어 있지 않으며, 잘못된 판단 기준을 그대로 둔 채 임계값만 조정합니다.\n- D: 리뷰어 추가는 약한 프롬프트를 땜질하는 안티패턴입니다. 비용이 늘고 같은 기준 부재 문제가 리뷰어에도 남습니다.\n\n시험 팁: False positive가 많다 → 포함 기준과 제외 사례를 명시한 explicit criteria가 1순위.","id":"scenario-b-54","task":"4.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":1,"stem":"The coordinator first extracts the bill of lading, confirming the booking number and three container numbers. It then spawns the DGD subagent with the prompt \"Extract the dangerous goods declaration for this shipment\" plus the packet's file path. The returned DGD records often have `booking_ref` set to null or to a guessed value, and list containers that are not on the bill. What is the most likely cause and best fix?","options":["The subagent lacks reference data; give it the `freight-reference` lookup tools and write access to the TMS so it can confirm bookings and containers by itself.","The subagent cannot see the coordinator's context; pass the booking number, confirmed containers, DGD page range, output schema, and success criteria in its prompt.","The subagent's model is too small for long packets; run the DGD subagent on the largest available model with extended thinking so it can infer the missing booking details.","The subagent was given too little history; forward the coordinator's full conversation transcript into the subagent prompt so it inherits everything learned so far."],"answer":1,"explanation":"서브에이전트는 context isolation 상태로 시작하며 오케스트레이터의 대화 이력이나 앞서 확인한 사실을 자동으로 상속하지 않습니다. 따라서 coordinator가 이미 확정한 booking 번호와 컨테이너 번호를 전달하지 않으면, 서브에이전트는 이를 추측하거나 null로 둘 수밖에 없습니다. 올바른 수정은 할당 시점에 필요한 것만 명시적으로 넘기는 것입니다. 즉 확정된 키 값, DGD가 있는 페이지 범위, 출력 스키마, success criteria(예: 컨테이너는 확정된 목록과 일치해야 함)를 전달합니다. 이것은 underpowered context 안티패턴에 대한 정석 처방입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 서브에이전트에게는 필요한 컨텍스트를 프롬프트로 명시 전달(최소 필요 + 명확한 기준) — Task Statement 1.3 · 출처: Section 4 (L17)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 쓰기 권한까지 주는 것은 least privilege 위반이며, 이미 coordinator가 아는 값을 다시 찾게 하는 우회입니다.\n- C: 모델 크기는 원인이 아닙니다. 전달되지 않은 정보는 아무리 추론해도 정확히 알 수 없습니다.\n- D: 전체 이력 전달은 컨텍스트 비대와 노이즈를 만들며, 필요한 것만 구조적으로 넘기라는 원칙에 어긋납니다.\n\n시험 팁: 서브에이전트가 \"이미 알려진 값\"을 모른다 → 프롬프트에 명시 전달. 이력 전체 전달은 오답.","id":"scenario-b-55","task":"1.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"After each DGD extraction, the same conversation receives a follow-up turn: \"Review your extraction above and fix any errors.\" This step changes less than 0.5% of records, yet a monthly audit finds errors in 6% of DGD hazard class and packing group fields. DGDs are about 3% of daily volume, and every error risks a refused container. What is the best way to improve the review step?","options":["Keep the same-conversation review but run it twice in a row, asking the second pass to look specifically for anything the first review pass may have missed or overlooked.","Use a separate review instance, without the generator's reasoning, to check the source DGD and extracted JSON against a field-level pass/fail checklist.","Remove the review step and instead enable extended thinking on the original extraction, so the model checks its own work before it calls the extraction tool.","Add an independent reviewer for all 40,000 daily documents, prompted to read the extraction and report any problems it finds in a short free-text comment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"같은 대화에서 자기 출력을 검토하게 하면 모델은 자신의 추론과 표현을 의도된 것으로 받아들이는 confirmation bias가 생겨 오류를 거의 찾지 못합니다. 고위험 필드에는 생성 과정의 추론을 공유하지 않는 independent review instance가 필요하며, 원문 DGD와 추출 JSON만 받아 평가하게 해야 합니다. 리뷰어 프롬프트는 \"문제를 찾아라\"가 아니라 hazard class와 UN 번호 일치, packing group 유효성 같은 explicit checklist와 필드별 structured pass/fail 결과를 써야 바로 수정 단계로 연결됩니다. DGD는 전체의 3%뿐이고 오류 비용이 크므로 multi-pass 비용이 정당화되는 전형적인 경우입니다. 위험도에 맞춰 리뷰 범위를 정하는 것도 설계의 일부입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 고위험 출력은 독립 인스턴스 + 명시적 checklist + 구조화된 critique — Task Statement 4.6 · 출처: Section 15 (L103)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 같은 컨텍스트에서 반복해도 같은 편향이 반복되므로 독립성이 생기지 않습니다.\n- C: 생성 단계의 추론 강화는 도움이 될 수 있지만, 독립 검증을 대체하지 못하고 같은 맹점을 공유합니다.\n- D: 저위험 문서까지 모두 리뷰하면 비용이 크게 늘고, 자유 텍스트의 모호한 리뷰는 일관된 수정으로 이어지지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: Self-review가 오류를 못 잡는다 → 독립 인스턴스 + 체크리스트, 고위험 부분에 집중.","id":"scenario-b-56","task":"4.6","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The bill-of-lading extraction subagent was given the full set of 14 pipeline tools, including `record_bill_of_lading`, `update_tms_record`, `file_customs_entry`, and `email_customer`, with `tool_choice` set to `auto`. Two problems appear: it sometimes calls `file_customs_entry` directly before validation has run, and on about 3% of documents it replies in prose instead of calling `record_bill_of_lading`. What is the best design change?","options":["Give the subagent only `record_bill_of_lading` and force it with `tool_choice` naming that tool; place the filing and TMS tools on a downstream agent run after validation.","Keep all 14 tools but set `tool_choice` to `{\"type\": \"any\"}`, so the subagent must call some tool on every turn and can no longer reply in plain prose.","Keep all 14 tools with `tool_choice` set to `auto`, and add a system-prompt rule that it must never call `file_customs_entry` and must always end by calling the extraction tool.","Keep all 14 tools with `tool_choice` set to `auto`, and add a hook that blocks `file_customs_entry` calls until the validation service has marked the record passed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"두 문제의 공통 원인은 역할에 맞지 않는 도구 분배와 느슨한 tool_choice 설정입니다. 추출 서브에이전트는 데이터를 포착하는 고정 단계이므로 least privilege 원칙에 따라 추출 도구만 받아야 하고, 신고나 TMS 갱신 같은 side effect 도구는 검증 뒤에 실행되는 하류 에이전트에 두어야 합니다. 또 매번 반드시 일어나야 하는 단일 단계에는 `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"record_bill_of_lading\"}`로 특정 도구를 강제하는 것이 맞으며, 이렇게 하면 산문 응답도 사라집니다. 도구가 적을수록 선택 오류도 줄어듭니다. A는 두 증상을 모두 구조적으로 제거합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 역할별 최소 도구 + 고정 단계는 특정 도구 강제(`tool`) — Task Statement 2.3 · 출처: Section 6 (L39, L41)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: `any`는 \"아무 도구나\"이므로 `file_customs_entry`를 고를 위험이 그대로 남습니다.\n- C: 프롬프트 규칙은 확률적이라 고위험 신고 경로를 보장하지 못하고, 불필요한 도구 노출도 그대로입니다.\n- D: hook은 조기 신고를 막을 수 있지만 산문 응답 문제를 해결하지 못하고, 필요 없는 13개 도구를 계속 노출합니다.\n\n시험 팁: 고정 추출 단계 = 해당 도구만 + `tool_choice` 특정 도구. `any`는 \"여러 유효 도구 중 하나\"일 때.","id":"scenario-b-57","task":"2.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":1,"stem":"The filing agent's system prompt states: \"Call `file_customs_entry` only after the record has passed validation and, for dangerous goods, only after a reviewer has approved it.\" Over the last quarter about 1 in 600 DG filings were still submitted without reviewer approval, usually when the agent saw a reviewer comment like \"looks fine, just checking the packing group.\" What is the most effective fix?","options":["Have the filing tool handler check the workflow store for passed validation and, for DG, a signed approval ID, refusing the call with a structured error otherwise.","Rewrite the instruction in capitals with the word NEVER, and add three examples of reviewer comments that do not count as approval to the agent's system prompt.","Add a separate reviewer model that reads the conversation before each filing call and judges whether the reviewer's comments amount to an approval of this particular shipment.","Lower the temperature of the filing agent to zero so that it follows the approval instruction consistently instead of interpreting ambiguous reviewer comments."],"answer":0,"explanation":"규제와 벌금이 걸린 단계에서 프롬프트 지시는 확률적이어서, 1/600처럼 드물지만 0이 아닌 위반이 반드시 남습니다. 고위험 경로에는 programmatic enforcement가 필요하며, filing 도구의 핸들러 자체가 workflow state store를 확인해 검증 통과 기록과 DG의 경우 서명된 approval ID가 없으면 호출을 거부해야 합니다. 거부 시에는 구조화된 오류를 반환해 에이전트가 사람 검토 대기로 handoff하도록 안내합니다. 이렇게 하면 \"looks fine\" 같은 모호한 코멘트를 해석할 여지 자체가 사라집니다. 승인은 대화 문맥이 아니라 시스템이 확인할 수 있는 상태여야 합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 반드시 지켜야 할 순서·전제 조건은 프롬프트가 아니라 코드 게이트로 강제 — Task Statement 1.4 · 출처: Section 5 (L28, L29)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 강조와 예시는 위반 빈도를 줄일 수는 있어도 0으로 만들지 못하는 prompt-only 해법입니다.\n- C: 또 다른 모델 판단을 겹치는 것은 확률적 판단을 하나 더 추가할 뿐 결정적 보장이 아닙니다.\n- D: temperature는 분산을 줄일 뿐, 모호한 코멘트를 승인으로 해석하는 판단 오류를 막지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"가끔이라도 절대 안 되는\" 순서 위반 → 프롬프트가 아니라 도구/코드 수준의 게이트.","id":"scenario-b-58","task":"1.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"Consolidated bills with 150+ container lines often fail to parse. The response has `stop_reason: \"max_tokens\"` and the JSON ends mid-array. The current code parses first, then on any parse error resends the identical request up to three times, and all three attempts fail the same way. Smaller bills are unaffected. What is the best fix?","options":["Check `stop_reason` before parsing; on `max_tokens`, retry with a higher limit, or extract container lines in page-range chunks and merge by container number.","Remove `strict: true` from the extraction tool so the model can return a partial but still parseable object when it approaches the output limit on large bills.","Add an instruction asking the model to keep all container line descriptions as short as possible so the full array fits inside the existing output token limit for each request.","Add a JSON repair step that closes any open brackets in truncated output so the parser succeeds, then pass the repaired record to the validation service."],"answer":0,"explanation":"strict 모드와 structured output은 스키마 준수를 보장하지만, `max_tokens` 잘림은 보장 범위 밖의 guarantee gap이라 JSON이 중간에 끊길 수 있습니다. 따라서 파싱보다 먼저 `stop_reason`을 확인해야 하며, `max_tokens`라면 같은 요청을 그대로 재시도하는 것은 같은 지점에서 다시 잘리므로 무의미합니다. 해법은 더 높은 출력 한도로 재요청하거나, 컨테이너 라인이 매우 많은 경우 페이지 범위별로 나눠 추출한 뒤 안정적인 키로 병합하는 것입니다. 이렇게 하면 대형 문서도 완전한 데이터로 처리됩니다. 원인이 길이라는 사실을 신호로 읽는 것이 핵심입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 먼저 `stop_reason`을 읽고, `max_tokens`면 한도 상향 또는 분할 — Task Statement 4.3 · 출처: Section 15 (L99)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: strict를 끄면 스키마 보장만 잃고, 출력 한도에 걸려 잘리는 근본 원인은 그대로입니다.\n- C: 설명을 짧게 해도 컨테이너 수가 더 많은 문서에서는 다시 잘리며, 필요한 데이터가 줄어들 위험도 있습니다.\n- D: 괄호만 닫으면 잘린 뒤의 컨테이너 라인이 조용히 누락된 \"유효한\" 레코드가 만들어져 silent data loss가 됩니다.\n\n시험 팁: 파싱 실패 + `max_tokens` → 같은 요청 반복 금지, 한도 상향이나 분할 추출.","id":"scenario-b-59","task":"4.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."},{"domain":4,"stem":"Strict tool use means 99.9% of extracted records pass schema validation, yet customs rejects 3% of pre-filings. Rejections cite container weights that do not add up to the stated gross weight, port of loading equal to port of discharge, and port codes that are well-formed but are not real UN/LOCODEs. These records currently go straight from schema validation to filing. What should the team add first?","options":["An `enum` listing every valid UN/LOCODE for the port fields in the schema, so the strict grammar can only generate real port codes during extraction.","A lower temperature and a system-prompt line telling the model to double-check weights and ports, since the extraction errors appear to be random variations between runs.","A second extraction run on every document with the same prompt, filing only the records where both runs produce identical values for every field.","Business-rule checks (weight sums within tolerance, distinct ports, LOCODE lookup) feeding specific errors to the retry loop, then the review desk."],"answer":3,"explanation":"스키마 검증은 타입과 필수 필드만 확인하는 floor일 뿐이며, 형식은 맞지만 의미가 틀린 값은 그대로 통과합니다. 고객사가 겪는 실패는 무게 합계 불일치, 출발항과 도착항 동일 같은 cross-field consistency 문제와, 형식은 맞지만 실제로 없는 코드라는 reference set 문제입니다. 따라서 schema 위에 business rule/semantic validation 층을 두어 허용 오차 내 무게 합계, 항구 상이성, LOCODE 참조 조회를 결정적으로 검사해야 합니다. 실패하면 구체적 오류를 retry loop에 넣고, 예산이 소진되면 review desk로 escalation합니다. 이렇게 하면 오류가 customs에 도달하기 전에 걸러집니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: Schema = floor, 운영 실패는 business rule·semantic 층에서 잡는다 — Task Statement 4.4 · 출처: Section 15 (L101, L102)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 수만 개 LOCODE enum은 비현실적이며, 무게 합계나 항구 동일성 같은 교차 필드 규칙은 enum으로 표현할 수 없습니다.\n- B: temperature는 분산만 줄일 뿐 grounding이나 교차 필드 오류를 해결하지 못하고, 프롬프트 지시는 검증을 대체하지 못합니다.\n- C: 두 번 추출해 일치를 확인하면 비용이 두 배가 되고, 같은 프롬프트의 체계적 오류는 두 번 모두 같게 나와 통과합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"스키마는 통과하는데 하류에서 거절\" → business rule·cross-field 검증 + 구체적 오류로 retry.","id":"scenario-b-60","task":"4.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a fictional freight forwarder, runs ManifestIQ, a pipeline that turns roughly 40,000 scanned and digital shipping documents per day into JSON records for its transport management system (TMS) and its customs pre-filing service. The documents are ocean bills of lading (master and house), air waybills, dangerous goods declarations (DGDs), packing lists, and proof-of-delivery receipts, often arriving together as one multi-document \"shipment packet\" PDF. A coordinator agent built on the Claude Agent SDK classifies each packet and spawns document-type-specific extraction subagents. Each extraction subagent returns data by calling an extraction tool such as `record_bill_of_lading`, whose input schema is defined with `strict: true`. An internal MCP server, `freight-reference`, exposes read-only lookups such as `lookup_un_number`, `lookup_carrier_scac`, and `lookup_port_unlocode`. A validation service applies schema checks plus business rules (ISO 6346 container check digits, weight totals, valid UN/LOCODEs) before anything reaches the TMS, and a human review desk handles exceptions. Customs pre-filings must be submitted at least 24 hours before vessel loading, and a wrong dangerous-goods record can lead to fines or a refused container. The team also plans a one-time backfill of 2.3 million archived documents. The goals are high-accuracy, schema-valid output, few false alarms for the review desk, and no unverified data reaching customs."}]};
